%feature("docstring")  casadi::Callback::has_jac_sparsity(casadi_int oind,
casadi_int iind) const "

Return sparsity of Jacobian of all input elements.

with respect to all output elements. Override has_jac_sparsity(oind, iind)
to return true and get_jac_sparsity() to return the pattern of the Jacobian
block of output ``oind`` with respect to input ``iind``. Without it the
block is assumed dense. Finite differencing exploits the pattern (fewer
evaluations) and the result of jacobian() carries it.



::

  >>> class Diag(Callback):
  ...   def __init__(self, name, opts={}):
  ...     Callback.__init__(self)
  ...     self.construct(name, opts)
  ...   def get_sparsity_in(self, i): return Sparsity.dense(3, 1)
  ...   def get_sparsity_out(self, i): return Sparsity.dense(3, 1)
  ...   def eval(self, arg):
  ...     return [arg[0]**2]
  ...   def has_jac_sparsity(self, oind, iind): return True
  ...   def get_jac_sparsity(self, oind, iind, symmetric): return Sparsity.diag(3)
  >>> f = Diag(\"f\", {\"enable_fd\": True})
  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\", 3)
  >>> J = jacobian(f(x), x)
  >>> J.sparsity()
  Sparsity(3x3,3nz)
  >>> Function(\"J\", [x], [J])([1, 2, 3])
  DM(
  [[2, 00, 00],
   [00, 4, 00],
   [00, 00, 6]])
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_ok

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/callback.hpp#L915
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/callback.hpp#L915-L915
";

