%feature("docstring")  casadi::Function::conditional(const std::string
&name, const std::vector< Function > &f, const Function &f_def, const Dict
&opts=Dict()) "

Create a function that selects one of several functions by an index input.

The result takes an index as first input followed by the inputs of the
branch functions. At evaluation the index is truncated to an integer k;
branch f[k] is evaluated when 0 <= k < len(f), otherwise ``f_def``. All
branches must have the same number of inputs and outputs; the signature
(names, shapes) is taken from ``f_def`` and arguments are projected when a
branch has a different sparsity. Derivatives are the derivatives of the
selected branch. Symbolic MX evaluation gives a call node; unlike if_else on
expressions, only the selected branch is evaluated numerically.



Parameters:
    name: Name of the result
    f: Branch functions, selected by index 0, 1,...
    f_def: Default branch for indices out of range
    opts: Function options



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> f0 = Function(\"f0\", [x], [x]); f1 = Function(\"f1\", [x], [x**2])
  >>> fdef = Function(\"fdef\", [x], [-x])
  >>> sw = Function.conditional(\"sw\", [f0, f1], fdef)
  >>> sw
  Function(sw:(i0,i1)->(o0) Switch)
  >>> sw(0, 3), sw(1, 3), sw(1.9, 3), sw(2, 3), sw(-1, 3)
  (DM(3), DM(9), DM(9), DM(-3), DM(-3))
  >>> sw(MX.sym(\"k\"), MX.sym(\"v\"))
  MX(sw(k, v){0})
  





See also: if_else

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1wm

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.hpp#L2169
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.cpp#L917-L924
";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::Function::conditional(const std::string
&name, const Function &f, const Dict &opts=Dict()) "

Create a function that calls ``f`` when its first input is nonzero and.

returns zeros otherwise

Shorthand for if_else with a zero-returning function of the same signature
as the false branch; evaluating with a zero condition skips ``f`` entirely.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x], [x**2])
  >>> c = Function.conditional(\"c\", f)
  >>> c, c(0, 3), c(1, 3)
  (Function(c:(i0,i1)->(o0) Switch), DM(0), DM(9))
  





See also: if_else

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1wn

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.hpp#L2199
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.cpp#L926-L941
";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::Function::bspline(const std::string &name,
const std::vector< std::vector< double > > &knots, const std::vector< double
> &coeffs, const std::vector< casadi_int > &degree, casadi_int m=1, const
Dict &opts=Dict()) "

Create a function evaluating a B-spline with known coefficients.

The result maps a point of dimension len(knots) (one column vector input) to
the m-dimensional spline value. Coefficients are stored flat in ``coeffs``
with the value dimension m fastest, then the first spline dimension, etc.;
the number of coefficients per dimension is len(knots[d]) - degree[d] - 1. A
mismatch between the lengths of ``knots`` and ``degree`` raises an error.
For data-driven splines or general interpolation see interpolant.



Parameters:
    name: Name of the result
    knots: Knot vector per dimension, non-decreasing, with repeated end knots
    coeffs: Flat coefficient list
    degree: Polynomial degree per dimension
    m: Dimension of the spline value
    opts: \"lookup_mode\" (per dimension: \"linear\", \"exact\", \"binary\") and Function options



::

  >>> f = Function.bspline(\"f\", [[0, 0, 0, 1, 2, 2, 2]], [0, 1, 2, 3], [2])
  >>> f
  Function(f:(i0)->(o0) MXFunction)
  >>> f(0), f(0.5), f(2)
  (DM(0), DM(0.875), DM(3))
  >>> g = Function.bspline(\"g\", [[0, 0, 1, 1], [0, 0, 1, 1]], [0, 1, 2, 3], [1, 1])
  >>> g([0.5, 0.5])
  DM(1.5)
  >>> try:
  ...   Function.bspline(\"f\", [[0, 0, 0, 1, 2, 2, 2]], [0, 1, 2, 3], [2, 2])
  ... except RuntimeError as e:
  ...   print(\"must match knot list length\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: interpolant, MX::bspline

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1wo

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.hpp#L2252
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.cpp#L943-L960
";

