%feature("docstring")  casadi::Function::check_name(const std::string &name)
"

Check whether a string is a valid function name.

A valid name starts with a letter and continues with letters, digits and
underscores, with no two consecutive underscores; it may not be one of the
keywords \"null\", \"jac\", \"hess\". Constructors and generate raise for
invalid names; names must be valid C identifiers because they appear in
generated code.



::

  >>> Function.check_name(\"f_1\"), Function.check_name(\"1f\")
  (True, False)
  >>> Function.check_name(\"a__b\"), Function.check_name(\"jac\"), Function.check_name(\"\")
  (False, False, False)
  





