%feature("docstring")  casadi::Callback::construct(const std::string &name,
const Dict &opts=Dict()) "

Construct the internal Function object.

The class constructor only creates a null pointer; this call creates the
Function. It must be called once from the subclass constructor, after all
data needed by
get_n_in/get_n_out/get_sparsity_in/get_sparsity_out/get_name_in/get_name_out
is set, because those methods are evaluated here. init() and finalize() are
called at the end. Calling it twice raises an error.



Parameters:
    name: Name of the Function
    opts: Function options, e.g. \"enable_fd\", \"fd_method\", \"fd_options\", \"enable_forward\", \"enable_reverse\", \"enable_jacobian\"



::

  >>> class Sq(Callback):
  ...   def __init__(self, name, opts={}):
  ...     Callback.__init__(self)
  ...     self.construct(name, opts)
  ...   def eval(self, arg):
  ...     return [arg[0]**2]
  >>> f = Sq(\"f\", {\"enable_fd\": True, \"fd_method\": \"forward\"})
  >>> f.name(), f.n_in(), f.n_out()
  ('f', 1, 1)
  >>> try:
  ...   f.construct(\"g\")
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Internal class already created\" in str(e))
  True
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_o5

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/callback.hpp#L292
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/callback.cpp#L36-L42
";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::Callback::init() "

Initialize the object.

Called from construct() after the inputs and outputs are known and the
options are processed, before finalize(). Override to allocate data; the
default does nothing.



::

  >>> class Sq(Callback):
  ...   def __init__(self, name, opts={}):
  ...     Callback.__init__(self)
  ...     print(\"before construct\")
  ...     self.construct(name, opts)
  ...     print(\"after construct\")
  ...   def init(self): print(\"init\", self.n_in())
  ...   def finalize(self): print(\"finalize\")
  ...   def eval(self, arg):
  ...     return [arg[0]**2]
  >>> f = Sq(\"f\")
  before construct
  init 1
  finalize
  after construct
  



