%feature("docstring")  casadi::Function::cache() const "

Get the derivative and map functions currently cached for this function.

jacobian, forward, reverse, wrap and serial map store their result in a
cache keyed by name (jac_f, fwd1_f, adj1_f, wrap_f, map3_f, ...). The cache
holds weak references: an entry stays only while some other reference keeps
the function alive. Option \"cache\" prepopulates it, e.g. with a hand-
written Jacobian.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x], [sin(x)])
  >>> f.cache()
  {}
  >>> J = f.jacobian()
  >>> list(f.cache().keys())
