%feature("docstring")  casadi::Function::get_function() const "

Get the names of the functions this function directly owns.

For an SXFunction or MXFunction: the functions called in its graph (an
MXFunction called with MX arguments is inlined and does not appear; SX
functions, solvers and calls made with never_inline do); for a map: the
mapped function; for a solver: its helper functions (e.g. nlp_f, nlp_jac_g
for nlpsol, which can also be code-generated with generate_dependencies).
Empty for leaf classes. Note that has_function only answers true for solver
objects; for SX and MX functions it is false even for names in this list.



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x], [sin(x)]).expand()
  >>> g = Function(\"g\", [x], [f(x) + 1])
  >>> g.get_function(), g.has_function(\"f\")
  (['f'], False)
  >>> g.get_function(\"f\")
  Function(f:(i0)->(o0) SXFunction)
  >>> try:
  ...   g.get_function(\"h\")
  ... except RuntimeError as e:
  ...   print(\"No such function 'h'\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: has_function, find_functions, oracle

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1y3

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.hpp#L3624
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.cpp#L2041-L2048
";

