%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::x() const "

Differential states.

Names of the variables of category ``x``, in category order. Equivalent to
``all(\"x\")``. A continuous variable becomes a differential state once its
time derivative is given a defining equation with ``eq``; it is an algebraic
variable ``z`` before that.



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> y = dae.add(\"y\")
  >>> dae.x(), dae.z()
  ([], ['x', 'y'])
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -y)
  >>> dae.x(), dae.z(), dae.nx()
  (['x'], ['y'], 1)
  





See also: z, q, nx, all, inputs

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_5f

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L309
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L309-L309
";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::y() const "

Outputs.

Names of the variables with causality ``\"output\"``, in category order.
Equivalent to ``all(\"y\")``. Outputs are also members of another category
(``x``, ``w``, ``z``, ...); ``outputs(\"y\")`` gives their expressions.



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\", \"output\")
  >>> y = dae.add(\"y\", \"output\")
  >>> w = dae.add(\"w\")
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -w)
  >>> dae.eq(w, x**2)
  >>> dae.eq(y, 2*x)
  >>> dae.y(), dae.x(), dae.w()
  (['x', 'y'], ['x'], ['der(x)', 'w', 'y'])
  >>> dae.outputs(\"y\")
  [MX(x), MX(y)]
  >>> dae.set_causality(\"y\", \"local\")
  >>> dae.y(), dae.ny()
  (['x'], 1)
  





See also: set_causality, set_all, ny, outputs

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2fu

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L358
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L358-L358
";

