%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::q() const "

Quadrature states.

Names of the variables of category ``q``: differential states that do not
appear in any right-hand side. Equivalent to ``all(\"q\")``. A state is only
placed here by ``set_category(name, \"q\")`` or automatically with the
constructor option ``\"detect_quad\"``.



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> q = dae.add(\"q\")
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -x)
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(q), x**2)
  >>> dae.x(), dae.q()
  (['x', 'q'], [])
  >>> dae.set_category(\"q\", \"q\")
  >>> dae.x(), dae.q(), dae.outputs(\"quad\")
  (['x'], ['q'], [MX(sq(x))])
  





See also: set_category, x, nq

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2fw

