";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::set_init(const std::string &name,
const MX &init_rhs) "

Specify the initial equation for a variable.

Sets ``name == init_rhs`` as initial equation, replacing any previous one
for the same variable. An empty ``init_rhs`` removes the initial equation.



Parameters:
    name: Model variable
    init_rhs: Expression in model variables, or an empty expression to remove



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> p = dae.add(\"p\", \"parameter\", \"tunable\")
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -x)
  >>> dae.init_lhs(), dae.init_rhs()
  ([], [])
  >>> dae.set_init(\"x\", 2*p)
  >>> dae.init_lhs(), dae.init_rhs()
  ([MX(x)], [MX((2.*p))])
  >>> dae.set_init(\"x\", MX())
  >>> dae.init_lhs(), dae.init_rhs()
