%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::eliminate(const std::string &cat)
"

Eliminate all dependent parameters.

Substitutes the variables of an acyclic category out of all model
expressions: ``\"c\"``, ``\"d\"`` or ``\"w\"`` (sorted first with ``sort``).
The variables keep existing but become ``calculated`` and the category is
left empty. For ``\"q\"`` the quadrature states are turned into regular
states ``x`` instead. Any other category is an error.



Parameters:
    cat: ``\"c\"``, ``\"d\"``, ``\"w\"`` or ``\"q\"``



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> w1 = dae.add(\"w1\")
  >>> w2 = dae.add(\"w2\")
  >>> dae.eq(w2, w1**2)
  >>> dae.eq(w1, 2*x)
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -w2)
  >>> dae.eliminate(\"w\")
  >>> dae.w(), dae.outputs(\"ode\"), dae.category(\"w1\")
  ([], [MX((-sq((2.*x))))], 'calculated')
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.eliminate(\"x\")
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Elimination not supported\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: sort, dependent_fun, lift

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2l1

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L1456
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L530-L536
";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::sort(const std::string &cat) "

Sort dependent parameters.

Reorders an acyclic category (``\"c\"``, ``\"d\"`` or ``\"w\"``) so that
every variable comes after the ones it depends on, using a block triangular
(Dulmage-Mendelsohn) decomposition of the dependency pattern. Vector-valued
variables are treated as a unit. Other categories are an error.



Parameters:
    cat: ``\"c\"``, ``\"d\"`` or ``\"w\"``



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> w1 = dae.add(\"w1\")
  >>> w2 = dae.add(\"w2\")
  >>> dae.eq(w2, w1**2)
  >>> dae.eq(w1, 2*x)
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -w2)
  >>> dae.w(), dae.wdef()
  (['w2', 'w1', 'der(x)'], [MX(sq(w1)), MX((2.*x)), MX((-w2))])
  >>> dae.sort(\"w\")
  >>> dae.w(), dae.wdef()
  (['w1', 'w2', 'der(x)'], [MX((2.*x)), MX(sq(w1)), MX((-w2))])
  





See also: eliminate, reorder

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2l2

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L1505
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L538-L544
";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::lift(bool lift_shared=true, bool
lift_calls=true) "

Lift problem formulation by extracting shared subexpressions.

Scans the right-hand sides of the ODEs, quadratures and algebraic equations
and replaces shared subexpressions and/or embedded function calls by new
dependent variables named ``w_<k>``, appended to ``w`` with their
definitions. The lifted definitions become part of ``wdef``; ``create`` with
``\"w\"`` as input then exposes them, and ``create`` with ``lifted_calls``
accounts for the calls in ``jac_wdef_w`` and Hessians. A warning is issued
when ``w`` is non-empty already, which is the case as soon as a state has an
ODE.



Parameters:
    lift_shared: Lift subexpressions that are used more than once
    lift_calls: Lift calls to embedded Function objects, including their arguments



::

  >>> a = MX.sym(\"a\")
  >>> F = Function(\"F\", [a], [sin(a) + a**2])
  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> y = dae.add(\"y\")
  >>> dae.eq(0, x - F(y))
  >>> dae.eq(0, y - F(x)**2 - F(y))
  >>> dae.lift()
  >>> dae.w()
  ['w_0', 'w_1', 'w_2', 'w_3', 'w_4']
  >>> dae.wdef()
  [MX(x), MX(y), MX(F(w_1){0}), MX(F(w_0){0}), MX(F(w_1){0})]
  >>> dae.outputs(\"alg\")
  [MX((-(w_0-w_2))), MX((-((w_1-sq(w_3))-w_4)))]
  >>> dae.create(\"f\", [\"z\", \"w\"], [\"alg\", \"wdef\"])
  Function(f:(z[2],w[5])->(alg[2],wdef[5]) MXFunction)
  





See also: eliminate, w, wdef

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2l3

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L1566
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L546-L552
";

