%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::add_fun(const std::string &name,
const std::vector< std::string > &arg, const std::vector< std::string >
&res, const Dict &opts=Dict()) "

Add a function from loaded expressions.

Creates a Function mapping the model variables ``arg`` to the binding
expressions of the dependent variables ``res`` and stores it in the
instance. Stored functions are listed by ``disp`` and retrieved with
``fun``.



Parameters:
    name: Function name; must not exist yet
    arg: Names of model variables used as inputs
    res: Names of dependent variables ``w``, whose definitions become the outputs; any other name is an error
    opts: Function options



Returns:
    The created function



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> w = dae.add(\"w\")
  >>> dae.eq(w, sin(x))
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -w)
  >>> f = dae.add_fun(\"wfun\", [\"x\"], [\"w\"])
  >>> f
  Function(wfun:(x)->(w) MXFunction)
  >>> dae.has_fun(\"wfun\"), dae.has_fun(\"nope\")
  (True, False)
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.add_fun(\"bad\", [\"x\"], [\"x\"])
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Cannot find dependent\" in str(e))
