%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::add_lc(const std::string &name,
const std::vector< std::string > &f_out) "

Add a named linear combination of output expressions.

Declares the name of a linear combination of output categories, so that
``create`` can produce its Hessian blocks ``hess_<name>_<in1>_<in2>`` with
the multipliers ``lam_<out>`` as extra inputs.



Parameters:
    name: Alphanumeric name
    f_out: Output categories in the combination, e.g. ``[\"ode\", \"alg\"]``; must be non-empty without duplicates



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> z = dae.add(\"z\")
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -x*z)
  >>> dae.eq(0, z - x**2)
  >>> dae.add_lc(\"gamma\", [\"ode\", \"alg\"])
  >>> H = dae.create(\"H\", [\"x\", \"z\", \"lam_ode\", \"lam_alg\"],
  ...                [\"hess_gamma_x_x\", \"hess_gamma_x_z\"])
  >>> H
  Function(H:(x,z,lam_ode,lam_alg)->(hess_gamma_x_x,hess_gamma_x_z) MXFunction)
  >>> H(1, 2, 1, 1)
  (DM(2), DM(-1))
  





See also: create

