%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::create(const std::string &name,
const std::vector< std::string > &name_in, const std::vector< std::string >
&name_out, const Dict &opts=Dict()) const "

Construct a function object, names provided.

The function factory: builds a Function whose inputs are variable categories
and whose outputs are equation categories or derivatives of them. Inputs are
any of ``t``, ``p``, ``d``, ``u``, ``x``, ``z``, ``q``, ``w``; constants
``c`` are never inputs, their current values (see ``set``) are substituted.
Outputs are ``ode``, ``alg``, ``quad``, ``zero``, ``ddef``, ``wdef``, ``y``.
Dependent variables ``w`` and parameters ``d`` not given as inputs are
substituted out. Derivative outputs use the Function factory naming with
underscores: ``jac_ode_x`` (Jacobian block) or ``hess_<lc>_x_x`` for a
linear combination declared with ``add_lc``, with the multipliers
``lam_ode``, ``lam_alg``, ... as inputs. The created function is a snapshot:
later changes to the instance do not affect it. For an imported FMU the
function evaluates the FMU binary.



Parameters:
    name: Name assigned to the resulting function object
    name_in: Names of all the inputs
    name_out: Names of all the outputs
    opts: Optional settings: Function options for a symbolic model; for an FMU also ``\"aux\"`` (names of variables reported in ``stats()`` after evaluation), ``\"enable_ad\"``, ``\"parallelization\"`` and the other FmuFunction options



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> z = dae.add(\"z\")
  >>> u = dae.add(\"u\", \"input\")
  >>> p = dae.add(\"p\", \"parameter\", \"tunable\")
  >>> c = dae.add(\"c\", \"parameter\", \"fixed\", dict(start=3))
  >>> w = dae.add(\"w\")
  >>> y = dae.add(\"y\", \"output\")
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -c*x + z*u)
  >>> dae.eq(0, x - p*z**2)
  >>> dae.eq(w, x + z)
  >>> dae.eq(y, w**2)
  >>> f = dae.create(\"f\", [\"x\", \"z\", \"u\", \"p\"], [\"ode\", \"alg\", \"y\"])
  >>> f
  Function(f:(x,z,u,p)->(ode,alg,y) MXFunction)
  >>> f(1, 2, 3, 4)
  (DM(3), DM(15), DM(9))
  >>> J = dae.create(\"J\", [\"x\", \"z\", \"u\", \"p\"], [\"jac_ode_x\", \"jac_alg_z\"])
  >>> J(1, 2, 3, 4)
  (DM(-3), DM(16))
  >>> dae.create(\"g\", [\"x\", \"z\", \"w\"], [\"ode\", \"wdef\"])
  Function(g:(x,z,w[3])->(ode,wdef[3]) MXFunction)
  >>> dae.create(\"s\", [\"x\", \"z\", \"u\", \"p\"], [\"ode\"], True)
  Function(s:(x,z,u,p)->(ode) SXFunction)
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.create(\"f\", [\"x\", \"z\", \"c\"], [\"ode\"])
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print('Cannot process \"c\" as input' in str(e))
  True
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.create(\"f\", [\"x\", \"z\"], [\"w\"])
  ... except Exception as e:
