%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::der(const MX &v) const "

Differentiate an expression with respect to time.

For a model variable ``x`` the derivative variable ``der(x)`` is returned,
created on first use (as an algebraic variable until ``eq`` gives it a
defining equation). For a concatenation of variables the derivatives are
concatenated; for a general expression the chain rule is applied through the
derivatives of the variables it depends on. The derivative of the
independent variable is 1 and that of parameters, constants, inputs and
discrete variables is 0. The expression must be a column vector in model
variables.



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> y = dae.add(\"y\")
  >>> p = dae.add(\"p\", \"parameter\", \"tunable\")
  >>> dae.der(x)
  MX(der(x))
  >>> dae.der(vertcat(x, y))
  MX(vertcat(der(x), der(y)))
  >>> dae.der(x*y + p)
  MX(((y*der(x))+(x*der(y))))
  >>> dae.der(p)
  MX(0)
  >>> dae.z()
  ['x', 'y', 'der(x)', 'der(y)']
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.der(vertcat(x, y).T)
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"must be a vector\" in str(e))
  True
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.der(MX.sym(\"foo\"))
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"No such variable\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: eq, der, var

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2ln

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L2363
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L912-L919
";

