%feature("docstring") casadi::DaeBuilder::DaeBuilder(const std::string
&name, const std::string &path="", const Dict &opts=Dict()) "

Construct a DaeBuilder instance.

Without ``path``, the instance starts empty and the model is built
symbolically with ``add`` and ``eq``. With ``path``, the model description
is imported immediately:



- a directory containing ``modelDescription.xml`` (an unzipped FMU),
- a ``.fmu`` archive (requires a build with ``WITH_GHC_FILESYSTEM=ON``; it is unzipped to a temporary directory that is removed once nothing references it any more),
- a ``.bmo`` Base Modelica file (requires the ``lacemodelica``  ModelicaParser plugin).



An imported standard FMU is not symbolic (``symbolic()`` is false):
equations are evaluated by calling the FMU binary, so ``create`` is
available but ``oracle``, ``eq``, ``eliminate`` etc. are not.



Parameters:
    name: Instance name; used as default function name prefix by ``create()``, ``transition()`` and ``export_fmu``
    path: Model to import, see above; empty for a symbolic model
    opts: Options (any other key is an error): ``\"debug\"`` (bool, false): print debug information during import and enable FMU logging ``\"fmutol\"`` (double, 0): tolerance passed to the FMU ``\"ignore_time\"`` (bool, false): do not expose the hidden time variable of an imported model that declares no independent variable ``\"detect_quad\"`` (bool, false): classify differential states that do not appear in any right-hand side as quadrature states ``q`` ``\"resource_serialize_mode\"`` (string): how an imported FMU is serialized with functions created from it, ``\"link\"`` or ``\"embed\"`` ``\"enable_ls_dae\"`` (bool, true): honour the DAE layered standard of an FMU ``\"enable_ls_serialization\"`` (bool, true): honour the serialization layered standard of an FMU
        ``\"debug\"`` (bool, false): print debug information during import and enable FMU logging
        ``\"fmutol\"`` (double, 0): tolerance passed to the FMU
        ``\"ignore_time\"`` (bool, false): do not expose the hidden time variable of an imported model that declares no independent variable
        ``\"detect_quad\"`` (bool, false): classify differential states that do not appear in any right-hand side as quadrature states ``q``
        ``\"resource_serialize_mode\"`` (string): how an imported FMU is serialized with functions created from it, ``\"link\"`` or ``\"embed\"``
        ``\"enable_ls_dae\"`` (bool, true): honour the DAE layered standard of an FMU
        ``\"enable_ls_serialization\"`` (bool, true): honour the serialization layered standard of an FMU



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"rocket\")
  >>> dae.name(), dae.symbolic(), dae.all()
  ('rocket', True, [])
  >>> try:
  ...   DaeBuilder(\"m\", \"/nonexistent/path\")
  ... except RuntimeError:
  ...   print(\"import failed\")
  import failed
  >>> try:
  ...   DaeBuilder(\"m\", \"\", dict(foo=True))
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"No such option\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: load_fmi_description, symbolic

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2ko

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L195
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L54-L57
";

