%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::set_causality(const std::string
&name, const std::string &val) "

Set the causality, if permitted.

The following changes are permitted:



- For controls ``u`` (variability ``\"continuous\"``, causality ``\"input\"``), free parameters ``p`` (variability ``\"tunable\"``, causality ``\"parameter\"``) and fixed parameters ``c`` (variability ``\"fixed\"``, causality ``\"parameter\"``), causality can only be changed indirectly, by updating the variability
- Add or remove an output ``y`` by setting the causality to ``\"output\"`` or ``\"local\"``, respectively



No other changes are permitted.



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> y = dae.add(\"y\", \"output\")
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -x)
  >>> dae.eq(y, 2*x)
  >>> dae.set_causality(\"y\", \"local\")
  >>> dae.set_causality(\"x\", \"output\")
  >>> dae.y(), dae.causality(\"y\")
  (['x'], 'local')
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.set_causality(\"x\", \"input\")
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Cannot change causality\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: causality, set_variability, set_category, set_all

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2c2

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L2639
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L612-L618
";

