%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::set_variability(const std::string
&name, const std::string &val) "

Set the variability, if permitted.

For controls ``u`` (variability ``\"continuous\"``, causality
``\"input\"``), free parameters ``p`` (variability ``\"tunable\"``,
causality ``\"parameter\"``) and fixed parameters ``c`` (variability
``\"fixed\"``, causality ``\"parameter\"``), update variability in order to
change the category. Causality is updated accordingly.

Other changes are not permitted.



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> u = dae.add(\"u\", \"input\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -u*x)
  >>> dae.set_variability(\"u\", \"fixed\")
  >>> dae.u(), dae.c(), dae.causality(\"u\")
  ([], ['u'], 'parameter')
  >>> dae.set_variability(\"u\", \"tunable\")
  >>> dae.p(), dae.causality(\"u\")
  (['u'], 'parameter')
  >>> dae.set_variability(\"u\", \"continuous\")
  >>> dae.u(), dae.causality(\"u\")
  (['u'], 'input')
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.set_variability(\"x\", \"discrete\")
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Cannot change variability\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: variability, set_causality, set_category

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2c3

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L2704
Implementation:
