%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::attribute(const std::string &a,
const std::string &name) const "

Get an attribute, single variable.

Numerical attribute of a scalar variable, selected by name: ``\"min\"``,
``\"max\"``, ``\"nominal\"``, ``\"start\"`` or ``\"value\"`` (the current
value, see ``get``). Any other attribute name, or a non-scalar variable, is
an error.



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\", dict(start=1, min=-2, nominal=10))
  >>> v = dae.add(\"v\", dict(dimension=[2], start=[1, 2]))
  >>> dae.attribute(\"start\", \"x\"), dae.attribute(\"min\", \"x\")
  (1.0, -2.0)
  >>> dae.attribute(\"start\", [\"x\", \"v\"]), dae.attribute(\"nominal\", [\"x\"])
  ([1.0, 1.0, 2.0], [10.0])
  >>> dae.set_attribute(\"min\", \"x\", -1)
  >>> dae.set_attribute(\"start\", [\"x\", \"v\"], [9, 8, 7])
  >>> dae.min(\"x\"), dae.start(\"v\")
  (-1.0, [8.0, 7.0])
  >>> try:
  ...   dae.attribute(\"unit\", \"x\")
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"No such enum\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: min, max, nominal, start, get

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2m6

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L3005
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L930-L937
";

