%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::set(const std::string &name,
double val) "

Set the current value, single value.

The current value is what ``get`` returns and what ``create`` substitutes
for the constants ``c``; set it before creating functions. A variable's
current value is initialized from its ``\"start\"`` option and is nan when
unset. A vector-valued variable gets all elements set.



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> c = dae.add(\"c\", \"parameter\", \"fixed\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\", dict(start=1))
  >>> v = dae.add(\"v\", dict(dimension=[2]))
  >>> s = dae.add(\"s\", dict(type=\"String\"))
  >>> dae.get(\"c\"), dae.get(\"x\"), dae.get(\"v\"), repr(dae.get(\"s\"))
  (nan, 1.0, [nan, nan], \"''\")
  >>> dae.set(\"c\", 2.5)
  >>> dae.set(\"v\", 1)
  >>> dae.set(\"s\", \"hello\")
  >>> dae.get([\"c\", \"v\", \"s\"])
  [2.5, [1.0, 1.0], 'hello']
  >>> dae.set([\"c\", \"x\"], [3, 4])
  >>> dae.set([\"v\"], [5, 6])
  >>> dae.get([\"c\", \"x\", \"v\"])
  [3.0, 4.0, [5.0, 6.0]]
  >>> dae.reset()
  >>> dae.get([\"c\", \"x\"])
  [nan, nan]
  



The value of a constant is baked into the functions created afterwards:



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> c = dae.add(\"c\", \"parameter\", \"fixed\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -c*x)
  >>> dae.set(\"c\", 3)
  >>> dae.create(\"f\", [\"x\"], [\"ode\"])(2)
  DM(-6)
  





See also: get, reset, start, c

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2ma

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L3196
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L1118-L1124
";

