%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::oracle(bool sx=false, bool
elim_w=false, bool lifted_calls=false) const "

Get the (cached) oracle, SX or MX.

The Function behind ``create`` for a symbolic model: inputs are all input
categories except ``c`` (whose current values are substituted), outputs are
all output categories, each as one concatenated vector (empty vectors for
empty categories). The oracle is cached and rebuilt when variables or
equations change. Not available for an imported FMU.



Parameters:
    sx: Return the SX expansion of the oracle instead of the MX graph
    elim_w: Substitute the dependent variables ``w`` out and drop them as input
    lifted_calls: Replace embedded function calls in ``wdef`` by zeros, for use with ``create`` with ``lifted_calls``; incompatible with ``elim_w``



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> w = dae.add(\"w\")
  >>> dae.eq(w, sin(x))
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -w)
  >>> f = dae.oracle()
  >>> f.name(), f.name_in()
  ('mx_oracle', ['t', 'p', 'd', 'w', 'u', 'x', 'z', 'q'])
  >>> f.name_out()
  ['ode', 'alg', 'quad', 'zero', 'ddef', 'wdef', 'y']
  >>> f.size1_in(\"w\"), f.size1_in(\"p\")
  (2, 0)
  >>> dae.oracle(True).class_name(), dae.oracle(False, True).name_in()
  ('SXFunction', ['t', 'p', 'd', 'u', 'x', 'z', 'q'])
  





See also: create, symbolic

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2mh

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L3393
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L862-L869
";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::DaeBuilder::jac_sparsity(const std::vector<
std::string > &onames, const std::vector< std::string > &inames) const "

Get Jacobian sparsity.

Structural dependency pattern of the variables ``onames`` with respect to
``inames``, one row per output name and one column per input name, taken
from the dependency information of the model structure. This information
comes from an imported model description or is computed by ``export_fmu``;
for a symbolically constructed model it is otherwise absent and the pattern
has no nonzeros.



Parameters:
    onames: Names of (derivative or output) variables
    inames: Names of variables to differentiate with respect to



Returns:
    Sparsity pattern of size ``len(onames)`` by ``len(inames)``



::

  >>> dae = DaeBuilder(\"m\")
  >>> x = dae.add(\"x\")
  >>> u = dae.add(\"u\", \"input\")
  >>> dae.eq(dae.der(x), -x*u)
  >>> dae.jac_sparsity([\"der(x)\"], [\"x\", \"u\"])
  Sparsity(1x2,0nz)
  





See also: load_fmi_description, export_fmu

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_6g

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.hpp#L3426
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/dae_builder.cpp#L1207-L1215
";

