%feature("docstring")  casadi::Function::map(const std::string &name, const
std::string &parallelization, casadi_int n, const std::vector< casadi_int >
&reduce_in, const std::vector< casadi_int > &reduce_out, const Dict
&opts=Dict()) const "

Map where some inputs are shared and some outputs are summed.

Inputs listed in ``reduce_in`` are not widened: the same value is used in
all n evaluations. Outputs listed in ``reduce_out`` are summed over the
evaluations instead of stacked. The index and name overloads build an
MXFunction around a plain map (``parallelization`` as in map; ``opts`` is
currently ignored). The boolean-mask overload creates a dedicated serial
MapSum node wrapped in an MXFunction built with ``opts``; masks must have
length n_in and n_out (an empty ``reduce_out`` means no reduction).



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); p = SX.sym(\"p\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x, p], [p*x, x], [\"x\", \"p\"], [\"y\", \"z\"])
  >>> F = f.map(\"F\", \"serial\", 3, [\"p\"], [\"y\"])
  >>> F
  Function(F:(x[1x3],p)->(y,z[1x3]) MXFunction)
  >>> F(DM([[1, 2, 3]]), 2)
  (DM(12), DM([[1, 2, 3]]))
  >>> f.map(3, [False, True], [True, False])(DM([[1, 2, 3]]), 2)
  (DM(12), DM([[1, 2, 3]]))
  





See also: map, mapsum

