%feature("docstring")  casadi::Function::export_code(const std::string
&lang, const std::string &fname, const Dict &options=Dict()) const "

Export the algorithm as source code in another language.

Only \"matlab\" is supported, and only for SXFunction and MXFunction without
free variables; other classes or languages raise an error. The code is a
plain MATLAB function with the same name that evaluates the algorithm on
numeric arguments, without any CasADi dependency. The file overload writes
to ``fname``, the other returns the code as a string.



Parameters:
    lang: \"matlab\"
    options: \"indent_level\" (integer)



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x], [sin(x)])
  >>> f.export_code(\"matlab\").splitlines()[0]
  'function [varargout] = f(varargin)'
  >>> try:
  ...   f.export_code(\"python\")
  ... except RuntimeError as e:
  ...   print(\"Only matlab language supported\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: generate

