%feature("docstring")  casadi::Function::sx_in(casadi_int iind) const "

Create fresh symbols with the names and sparsity patterns of the inputs.

Convenient for calling the function symbolically or for building a wrapper:
f(f.mx_in()) is an MX expression of the outputs. Each call creates new
symbols; they are not the symbols the function was constructed from. All
inputs (no argument), one by index, or one by name.



::

  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [SX.sym(\"a\"), SX.sym(\"B\", Sparsity.diag(2))], [SX(0)],
  ...              [\"a\", \"B\"], [\"r\"])
  >>> f.sx_in()
  [SX(a), SX(
  [[B_0, 00],
   [00, B_1]])]
  >>> f.mx_in(1), f.mx_in(\"a\").shape
  (MX(B), (1, 1))
  >>> f.sx_out(), f.mx_out(0)
  ([SX(r)], MX(r))
  





See also: sx_out, mx_out, sparsity_in

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1x4

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.hpp#L2829
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.cpp#L1749-L1755
";

