%feature("docstring")  casadi::Function::nz_from_in(const std::vector< DM >
&arg) const "

Convert between a list of input/output matrices and one flat list of.

nonzeros

nz_from_in flattens a list of n_in() DM arguments (shape rules as in call)
into the concatenated nonzeros, in input order and column-major within each
input; nz_to_in does the reverse, the list must have exactly nnz_in()
entries. nz_from_out and nz_to_out do the same for the outputs with
nnz_out(). This is the memory layout that generated C code and
FunctionBuffer use.



::

  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [SX.sym(\"x\"), SX.sym(\"D\", Sparsity.diag(2))], [SX(0)])
  >>> f.nz_from_in([1, DM([[2, 0], [0, 3]])])
  [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]
  >>> f.nz_to_in([1, 2, 3])
  [DM(1), DM(
  [[2, 00],
   [00, 3]])]
  >>> try:
  ...   f.nz_to_in([1, 2])
  ... except RuntimeError as e:
  ...   print(\"Dimension mismatch. Expecting 3, got 2\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: convert_in, generate_in, FunctionBuffer

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1x6

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.hpp#L2910
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/function.cpp#L1797-L1799
";

