%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericExpressionCommon::pow(const ExType &x,
const ExType &y) "

Elementwise power: (x,y) -> x.^y.

Elementwise; shape rules as for plus. Named power in Python, where the **
operator maps to it as well. A constant exponent is simplified symbolically:
integer powers become repeated squaring and multiplication, 0.5 becomes
sqrt, -1 a reciprocal, other constants a constpow operation. Structural
zeros of ``x`` stay zero for a nonzero exponent; x**0 is dense (0**0 == 1).



::

  >>> power(DM([1, 2, 3]), 2)
  DM([1, 4, 9])
  >>> DM([1, 2, 3])**DM([3, 2, 1]), 2**DM([1, 2, 3])
  (DM([1, 4, 3]), DM([2, 4, 8]))
  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> x**2, x**3, x**-1, x**x
  (SX(sq(x)), SX((x*sq(x))), SX((1./x)), SX(pow(x,x)))
  >>> x**2.5
  SX(pow(x,2.5))
  





See also: sq, sqrt, constpow, mpower

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_pp

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L1420
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L1420-L1422
";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericExpressionCommon::mod(const ExType &x,
const ExType &y) "

Remainder after division: (x,y) -> fmod(x,y)

This Function follows the convention of
https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/math/fmod:  the result has the sign
of ``x`` and magnitude below |y|.

This is equivalent to Python's numpy.fmod and Matlab's rem. It differs from
the Python operator x % y on these objects, which follows the Python
convention x - y*floor(x/y) (result with the sign of ``y``). Elementwise,
shape rules as for plus; structural zeros of ``x`` stay zero. A zero divisor
gives NaN.



::

  >>> fmod(DM([5, 5, -5, -5]), DM([3, -3, 3, -3]))
  DM([2, 2, -2, -2])
  >>> DM([5, 5, -5, -5]) % DM([3, -3, 3, -3])
  DM([2, -1, 1, -2])
  >>> fmod(SX.sym(\"x\"), 2), SX.sym(\"x\") % 2
  (SX(fmod(x,2)), SX((x-(2.*floor((x/2))))))
  





See also: remainder, floor  Extra doc:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_pq



Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L1463
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L1463-L1465
";

