%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericExpressionCommon::constpow(const
ExType &x, const ExType &y) "

Elementwise power with const power: (x,y) -> x^y with y constant.

Same value as pow, but the exponent is assumed constant: the derivative with
respect to ``y`` is taken as zero. pow itself produces this operation for a
non- integer constant exponent, so it is rarely needed directly. Passing a
symbolic exponent gives a wrong derivative for MX; SX falls back to pow.



::

  >>> constpow(DM(2), 3)
  DM(8)
  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> constpow(x, 2.5), jacobian(constpow(x, 2.5), x)
  (MX(pow(x,2.5)), MX((2.5*pow(x,1.5))))
  





See also: pow

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2om

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L1782
Implementation:
