";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericExpressionCommon::hypot(const ExType
&x, const ExType &y) "

Precision variant for 2 norm: (x,y) -> sqrt(x^2+y^2)

Elementwise; avoids the overflow and underflow of forming the squares, as C
hypot. Shape rules as for plus; the result is structurally zero where both
operands are.



::

  >>> hypot(DM(3), DM(4))
  DM(5)
  >>> hypot(DM(1e200), DM(1e200))
  DM(1.41421e+200)
  >>> hypot(SX.sym(\"x\"), SX.sym(\"y\"))
  SX(hypot(x,y))
  





See also: norm_2

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_pw

