%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericExpressionCommon::is_equal(const
ExType &x, const ExType &y, casadi_int depth=0) "

Check if two nodes are equivalent up to a given depth.

Depth=0 checks if the expressions are identical, i.e. points to the same
node.

a = x*x b = x*x

is_equal(a,b,0) will return false, but is_equal(a,b,1) will return true

Returns a plain boolean, unlike the elementwise comparison eq. With
``depth`` > 0 two different nodes are equivalent when they have the same
operation and their dependencies are equivalent up to depth-1. For SX and DM
matrices the test is applied entry by entry; matrices of different shape
raise an error, and for DM it is value equality. Both arguments must be of
the same type.



Parameters:
    x: First expression
    y: Second expression
    depth: Number of levels of the expression graph to compare, 0 for identity



::

   >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
   >>> is_equal(x, x), is_equal(x, SX.sym(\"x\"))
   (True, False)
   >>> is_equal(x*x, x*x), is_equal(x*x, x*x, 1)
   (False, True)
   >>> is_equal(DM([1, 2]), DM([1, 2])), is_equal(DM([1, 2]), DM([1, 3]))
   (True, False)
   >>> y = MX.sym(\"y\")
   >>> is_equal(y * y, y * y), is_equal(y * y, y * y, 1)
   (False, True)





See also: eq

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_pv

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L1713
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L1713-L1715
";

