%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericExpressionCommon::plus(const ExType
&x, const ExType &y) "

Addition: (x,y) -> x + y.

Elementwise sum. The shape rules below hold for every binary operation in
this group (minus, times, rdivide, the comparisons, logic_and, ...):

- both operands have the same shape, or
- one operand is a scalar (1-by-1), which is combined with every element, or
- the operands have the same number of rows and the column count of one is a multiple of the other's; the narrower one is repeated horizontally (so a column vector can be added to every column of a matrix, but a row vector cannot be added to every row). Any other combination raises an error; there is no further broadcasting. Empty matrices follow the same rules and give an empty result.



The result is sparse where both operands are structurally zero; an entry
that is a structural zero in only one operand becomes an explicit value.
Operations that map (0, y) or (x, 0) to a nonzero, such as x + 1 or cos,
densify the result. Numeric (DM) operands are evaluated, symbolic ones (SX,
MX) build an expression; DM and SX or MX can be mixed, SX and MX cannot.



::

  >>> plus(DM([1, 2]), DM([10, 20]))
  DM([11, 22])
  >>> DM([1, 2]) + 1
  DM([2, 3])
  >>> DM.eye(2) + DM.eye(2)
  DM(
  [[2, 00],
   [00, 2]])
  >>> DM.eye(2) + 1
  DM(
  [[2, 1],
   [1, 2]])
  >>> SX.sym(\"x\", 2, 2) + SX.sym(\"y\", 2)
  SX(
  [[(x_0+y_0), (x_2+y_0)],
   [(x_1+y_1), (x_3+y_1)]])
  >>> (MX.sym(\"x\", 2, 0) + 1).shape
  (2, 0)
  >>> DM.ones(2, 2) + DM.ones(1, 2)
  Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
  RuntimeError: ...Dimension mismatch...
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_on

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L128
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L128-L130
";

