%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::interp1d(const
std::vector< double > &x, const MatType &v, const std::vector< double > &xq,
const std::string &mode, bool equidistant=false) "

Performs 1d linear interpolation.

The data points are (x[i], v[i, :]): row i of ``v`` holds the values at
abscissa x[i], so ``v`` has as many rows as ``x`` has entries and every
column is interpolated independently. The result has one row per query point
xq[j].

Queries outside the range of ``x`` are clamped to the first or last data
point (no extrapolation). The result is a constant sparse matrix times
``v``, so for symbolic ``v`` the expression is linear in ``v``.



Parameters:
    x: Abscissae, strictly increasing, at least two entries
    v: Data values, x.size()-by-m
    xq: Query abscissae, any order
    mode: \"linear\" (interpolate), \"floor\" (value at the data point at or below the query) or \"ceil\" (at or above); any other string raises an error
    equidistant: When true, ``x`` is assumed uniformly spaced and the interval is located arithmetically from x[0] and x[1] instead of by search



Returns:
    Matrix of size xq.size()-by-m



::

  >>> interp1d([0, 1, 2], DM([0, 10, 20]), [0.5, 1.5])
  DM([5, 15])
  >>> interp1d([0, 1, 2], DM([0, 10, 20]), [0.5, 1.5], \"floor\")
  DM([0, 10])
  >>> interp1d([0, 1, 2], DM([[0, 1], [10, 11], [20, 21]]), [0.5, 2])
  DM(
  [[5, 6],
   [20, 21]])
  >>> interp1d([0, 1, 2], DM([0, 10, 20]), [-1, 3])
  DM([0, 20])
  >>> interp1d([0, 1, 2], SX.sym(\"v\", 3), [0.5])
  SX(@1=0.5, ((@1*v_0)+(@1*v_1)))
  





See also: interpolant

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1bh

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L603
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L603-L606
";

