%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::sumsqr(const MatType &x)
"

Calculate sum of squares: sum_ij X_ij^2.

Defined as dot(x, x) for a matrix of any shape; structural zeros contribute
nothing. Prefer this over norm_2(x)**2 in objectives: it is smooth
everywhere.



::

  >>> sumsqr(DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]))
  DM(30)
  >>> sumsqr(SX.sym(\"x\", 2))
  SX((sq(x_0)+sq(x_1)))
  >>> sumsqr(MX.sym(\"x\", 2))
  MX(dot(x, x))
  





See also: dot, norm_2, norm_fro

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1bq

