%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::cross(const MatType &a,
const MatType &b, casadi_int dim=-1) "

Matlab's ``cross`` command.

Cross product of 3-vectors. ``a`` and ``b`` must have the same shape and one
of the dimensions must be 3; for 3-by-n or n-by-3 matrices the products are
taken per column or per row respectively.



Parameters:
    dim: 1 to take the products along the rows (3-by-n input), 2 along the columns, -1 (default) to pick the dimension of length 3 (rows first)



::

  >>> cross(DM([1, 0, 0]), DM([0, 1, 0]))
  DM([0, 0, 1])
  >>> cross(DM([[1, 0, 0], [0, 1, 0]]), DM([[0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]]))
  DM(
  [[0, 0, 1],
   [1, 0, 0]])
  >>> cross(SX.sym(\"a\", 3), SX.sym(\"b\", 3))
  SX([((a_1*b_2)-(a_2*b_1)), ((a_2*b_0)-(a_0*b_2)), ((a_0*b_1)-(a_1*b_0))])
  





See also: skew, dot

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1bu

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1078
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1078-L1080
";

