Inverse of skew: for a 3-by-3 matrix S, returns 0.5*[S(2,1)-S(1,2);
S(0,2)-S(2,0); S(1,0)-S(0,1)], which recovers ``a`` from skew(a). A
non-3-by-3 argument raises an error.



