%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::tril2symm(const MatType
&a) "

Convert a lower triangular matrix to a symmetric one.

Returns a + a' - diag(diag(a)), i.e. mirrors the strictly lower part to the
upper part. The argument must be square and have no structural nonzeros
above the diagonal (a dense matrix is rejected even if numerically lower
triangular).



::

  >>> L = DM(Sparsity.lower(3), [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6])
  >>> tril2symm(L)
  DM(
  [[1, 2, 3],
   [2, 4, 5],
   [3, 5, 6]])
  >>> tril2symm(SX.sym(\"L\", Sparsity.lower(2)))
  SX(
  [[L_0, L_1],
   [L_1, L_2]])
  





See also: triu2symm, tril, is_tril

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1c2

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1329
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1329-L1329
";

