%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::diff(const MatType &x,
casadi_int n=1, casadi_int axis=-1) "

Returns difference (n-th order) along given axis (MATLAB convention)

Each pass subtracts neighbouring rows (axis 0) or columns (axis 1),
shrinking that dimension by one; ``n`` passes are applied. With axis -1 the
first non-singleton dimension is used (columns for a row vector, rows
otherwise) and, as in MATLAB, a scalar gives an empty 0-by-0 result.



Parameters:
    n: Order, at least 1
    axis: 0 (rows), 1 (columns) or -1 (automatic)



::

  >>> diff(DM([1, 4, 9, 16]))
  DM([3, 5, 7])
  >>> diff(DM([1, 4, 9, 16]), 2)
  DM([2, 2])
  >>> diff(DM([[1, 2], [4, 8], [9, 10]]), 1, 1)
  DM([1, 4, 1])
  >>> diff(SX.sym(\"x\", 3))
  SX([(x_1-x_0), (x_2-x_1)])
  >>> diff(DM(3)).dim()
  '0x0'
  





See also: cumsum

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1c8

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1499
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1499-L1501
";

