%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::is_quadratic(const
MatType &expr, const MatType &var) "

Is expr quadratic in var?

Defined as: gradient(expr, var) is linear in ``var``; hence ``expr`` must be
scalar. False negatives are possible (an expression may not be recognised as
quadratic while it really is), see is_linear for the structural nature of
the check. Linear and constant expressions count as quadratic.



::

  * >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  * >>> is_quadratic(x*y + x**2, vertcat(x, y)), is_quadratic(x**3, x)
  * (True, False)
  * >>> is_quadratic(x, x)
  * True
  * 





See also: is_linear, quadratic_coeff

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1d1

