%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::quadratic_coeff(const
MatType &expr, const MatType &var, MatType &A, MatType &b, MatType &c, bool
check=true) "

Recognizes quadratic form in scalar expression.

1/2*x' A x + b' x + c

e = 0.5*bilin(A,x,x)+dot(b,x)+c

Returns A = hessian(expr, var), b = jacobian(expr, var) at var = 0 as a
column, and c = expr at var = 0. A non-scalar ``expr`` raises an error.



Parameters:
    check[in]: When true (default), A is checked to be independent of x and an error is raised otherwise (\"called on non-quadratic expression\"). Provided to deal with false positive dependency checks.



::

  * >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  * >>> A, b, c = quadratic_coeff(x**2 + 2*x*y + 3*x + 4, vertcat(x, y))
  * >>> A
  * SX(@1=2,
  * [[@1, @1],
  *  [@1, 00]])
  * >>> b, c
  * (SX([3, 0]), SX(4))
  * >>> try: quadratic_coeff(x**3, x)
  * ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  * error
  * 





See also: linear_coeff, is_quadratic, hessian

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1d2

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2897
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2897-L2900
";

