%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::gradient(const MatType
&ex, const MatType &arg, const Dict &opts=Dict()) "

Calculate the gradient of an expression.

Computed with one reverse-mode sweep (jtimes with tr true) and projected
onto the sparsity of ``arg:`` the result has the shape and pattern of
``arg``, also for a matrix ``arg``. A non-scalar ``ex`` raises an error (use
jacobian).



Parameters:
    ex: Scalar expression to take the gradient of
    arg: Symbolic expression (any shape)
    opts: Options, see jacobian



Returns:
    Matrix with the sparsity of ``arg``



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> gradient(x*y + x**2, vertcat(x, y))
  SX([((2.*x)+y), x])
  >>> gradient(x**2, vertcat(x, y))
  SX([(2.*x), 0])
  >>> A = SX.sym(\"A\", 2, 2)
  >>> gradient(sumsqr(A), A)
  SX(
  [[(2.*A_0), (2.*A_2)],
   [(2.*A_1), (2.*A_3)]])
  





See also: jacobian, hessian, jtimes

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_23x

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2512
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2512-L2514
";

