%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::linearize(const MatType
&f, const MatType &x, const MatType &x0, const Dict &opts=Dict()) "

Linearize an expression.

[DEPRECATED] confusing behaviour

This function linearizes an expression around a point x0, using x as delta
around that point:

linearize(sin(x),x,x0) -> sin(x0)+cos(x0)*x

``x0`` must have the shape of ``x`` or be a scalar (broadcast). For a
variant that returns sin(x0)+cos(x0)*(x-x0), see taylor.



::

  * >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  * >>> linearize(sin(x), x, y)
  * SX((sin(y)+(cos(y)*x)))
  * 





