%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::casadi_mpower "

Matrix power x^n.

For a square matrix ``x`` and a constant integer scalar ``n``, computes the
repeated matrix product by squaring. n == 0 gives the (sparse) identity,
negative ``n`` gives the inverse of the positive power (via inv). If both
arguments are scalar, this is the elementwise pow. A non-integer or symbolic
``n`` for a matrix raises an error.



::

  >>> A = DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]])
  >>> mpower(A, 2)
  DM(
  [[7, 10],
   [15, 22]])
  >>> mpower(A, 0)
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [00, 1]])
  >>> mpower(A, -1)
  DM(
  [[-2, 1],
   [1.5, -0.5]])
  >>> mpower(DM(2), 0.5)
  DM(1.41421)
  >>> try: mpower(A, 0.5)
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  





See also: mtimes, inv, expm

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1bi

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L656
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L656-L658
";

