%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::sym(const std::string
&name, casadi_int nrow=1, casadi_int ncol=1) "

Create an nrow-by-ncol symbolic primitive.

Creates a new, dense symbol; two symbols with the same name are still
different symbols. For SX each entry is a separate scalar symbol named
name_k (k the column-major index), while an MX symbol is a single node with
the given name. Only SX and MX have symbols; DM.sym raises an error.



Parameters:
    name: Name used for printing. For SX, a name of the form \"[a,b,c]\" assigns individual names to the numel() entries.
    nrow: Number of rows, default 1
    ncol: Number of columns, default 1



::

  >>> SX.sym(\"x\"), MX.sym(\"x\", 2, 3).dim()
  (SX(x), '2x3')
  >>> SX.sym(\"x\", 2, 2)
  SX(
  [[x_0, x_2],
   [x_1, x_3]])
  >>> SX.sym(\"[a,b,c]\", 3)
  SX([a, b, c])
  >>> is_equal(SX.sym(\"x\"), SX.sym(\"x\"))
  False
  





See also: symvar, zeros, ones

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1da

