%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::einstein(const MatType
&A, const MatType &B, const MatType &C, const std::vector< casadi_int >
&dim_a, const std::vector< casadi_int > &dim_b, const std::vector<
casadi_int > &dim_c, const std::vector< casadi_int > &a, const std::vector<
casadi_int > &b, const std::vector< casadi_int > &c) "

Compute any contraction of two dense tensors, using index/einstein notation.

Given two tensors, A and B, computes a third tensor C such that:

C_c = A_a * B_b

With a, b, c representing einstein indices. Instead of the classical index
labels i,j,k,... we employ -1,-2,-3,... An index that appears in a or b but
not in c is summed over.

A, B, C are represented as CasADi column vectors (column-major flattening),
with dim_a, dim_b, dim_c indicating their tensorial dimensions. The product
of dim_a must equal the number of elements of A, and likewise for B and C.

In the overload with an explicit ``C`` argument, the contraction is added to
``C``.



::

  >>> A = DM([1, 2, 3, 4])
  >>> einstein(A, A, [2, 2], [2, 2], [2, 2], [-1, -2], [-2, -3], [-1, -3])
  DM([7, 10, 15, 22])
  >>> mtimes(DM([[1, 3], [2, 4]]), DM([[1, 3], [2, 4]]))
  DM(
  [[7, 15],
   [10, 22]])
  >>> einstein(DM([1, 2, 3]), DM([4, 5, 6]), [3], [3], [], [-1], [-1], [])
  DM(32)
  





See also: mtimes, dot

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1bk

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L735
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L735-L741
";

