%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::mmin(const MatType &x) "

Smallest element in a matrix.

Over all entries, structural zeros included (so a sparse matrix with only
positive nonzeros has minimum 0). An empty matrix gives an empty 0-by-0
result. For SX a chain of fmin operations is built; for MX a single node.



::

  >>> mmin(DM([[3, -1], [2, 5]])), mmax(DM([[3, -1], [2, 5]]))
  (DM(-1), DM(5))
  >>> mmin(DM(Sparsity.diag(2), [3, 4]))
  DM(0)
  >>> mmin(SX.sym(\"x\", 3))
  SX(fmin(fmin(x_0,x_1),x_2))
  





See also: mmax, fmin, norm_inf

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1d8

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L3424
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L3424-L3426
";

