%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::logsumexp(const MatType
&x) "

x -> log(sum_i exp(x_i))

Can be used to achieve a smooth max.

The argument must be a dense column vector; a scalar is returned unchanged.
Implementations for DM/SX/MX are hardened against overflow by shifting with
the largest entry. Implementations for DM/MX are more accurate with log1p
(*).

(*) https://nhigham.com/2021/01/05/what-is-the-log-sum-exp-function/



::

  >>> logsumexp(DM([1, 2, 3]))
  DM(3.40761)
  >>> logsumexp(DM([1000, 1000]))
  DM(1000.69)
  >>> logsumexp(MX.sym(\"x\", 3))
  MX(logsumexp(x))
  >>> try: logsumexp(DM([1, 2, 3]).T)
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  





See also: mmax

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1br

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L989
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L989-L991
";

