%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::det(const MatType &A) "

Matrix determinant (experimental)

For DM and SX the determinant is formed by minor expansion along the
sparsest row or column (a 2-by-2 directly, a scalar is returned as is); the
cost grows quickly with the matrix size. For MX a determinant node is
created that is evaluated through the 'qr' linear solver. A non-square
argument raises an error.



::

  >>> det(DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]))
  DM(-2)
  >>> det(SX.sym(\"A\", 2, 2))
  SX(((A_0*A_3)-(A_2*A_1)))
  >>> det(MX.sym(\"A\", 2, 2))
  MX(det(A))
  





See also: inv, inv_minor

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1bx

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1153
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1153-L1153
";

