%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::inv(const MatType &A) "

Matrix inverse.

Computed as solve(A, eye(n)), see solve for the algorithm. A non- square
argument raises an error. A numerically singular DM does not raise; the
result contains inf or nan. For MX the result is a solve node.



::

  >>> inv(DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]))
  DM(
  [[-2, 1],
   [1.5, -0.5]])
  >>> inv(SX.sym(\"A\", 2, 2))
  SX(@1=((A_0*A_3)-(A_2*A_1)),
  [[(A_3/@1), (-(A_2/@1))],
   [(-(A_1/@1)), (A_0/@1)]])
  >>> inv(DM(Sparsity.diag(2), [2, 4]))
  DM(
  [[0.5, 00],
   [00, 0.25]])
  





See also: solve, pinv, det, mldivide

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1bz

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1239
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1239-L1241
";

