%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::norm_2(const MatType &x)
"

2-norm

For a vector (row or column) this is the Euclidean norm, identical to
norm_fro. For a matrix argument DM and SX raise an error (use norm_fro if
that is what you meant); MX creates a spectral-norm node that cannot be
evaluated. Not differentiable at x == 0; use sumsqr in objectives where
possible.



::

  >>> norm_2(DM([3, 4]))
  DM(5)
  >>> norm_2(MX.sym(\"x\", 2))
  MX(||x||_F)
  >>> try: norm_2(DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]))
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  





See also: norm_fro, norm_1, norm_inf, sumsqr

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1c5

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1410
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1410-L1410
";

