%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::cumsum(const MatType &x,
casadi_int axis=-1) "

Returns cumulative sum along given axis (MATLAB convention)

Running sum down the rows (axis 0) or along the columns (axis 1); the shape
is preserved. With axis -1, the columns are summed for a row vector and the
rows otherwise.



::

  >>> cumsum(DM([1, 2, 3]))
  DM([1, 3, 6])
  >>> cumsum(DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]))
  DM(
  [[1, 2],
   [4, 6]])
  >>> cumsum(DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]), 1)
  DM(
  [[1, 3],
   [3, 7]])
  >>> cumsum(SX.sym(\"x\", 3))
  SX(@1=(x_1+x_0), [x_0, @1, (x_2+@1)])
  





See also: diff, sum1, sum2

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1c9

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1540
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1540-L1542
";

