%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::dot(const MatType &x,
const MatType &y) "

Inner product of two matrices.

Sum of the elementwise products over all entries, with ``x`` and ``y`` of
the same shape (a matrix is treated as the vector of its entries). Only
entries that are structurally nonzero in both arguments contribute. A shape
mismatch raises an error.



::

  >>> dot(DM([1, 2]), DM([3, 4]))
  DM(11)
  >>> dot(DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]), DM([[1, 1], [1, 1]]))
  DM(10)
  >>> dot(DM(Sparsity.diag(2), [1, 2]), DM([[1, 1], [1, 1]]))
  DM(3)
  >>> dot(SX.sym(\"x\", 2), SX.sym(\"y\", 2))
  SX(((x_0*y_0)+(x_1*y_1)))
  





See also: mtimes, sumsqr, bilin

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1ca

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1575
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1575-L1577
";

