%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::nullspace(const MatType
&A) "

Computes the nullspace of a matrix A.

Finds Z m-by-(m-n) such that AZ = 0 with A n-by-m with m >= n (a matrix with
more rows than columns raises an error).

Assumes A is full rank. Computed with Householder reflections, dense; for MX
the SX algorithm is embedded as a function call node.

Inspired by Numerical Methods in Scientific Computing by Ake Bjorck



::

  >>> A = DM([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]])
  >>> Z = nullspace(A)
  >>> Z.dim(), float(norm_1(mtimes(A, Z))) < 1e-12
  ('3x1', True)
  





See also: qr, pinv

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1cb

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1606
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1606-L1608
";

