%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::polyval(const MatType
&p, const MatType &x) "

Evaluate a polynomial with coefficients p in x.

Horner evaluation of p[0]*x^(n-1) + ... + p[n-2]*x + p[n-1]: the first
coefficient belongs to the highest power, as in MATLAB's polyval. The
polynomial is applied to every structurally nonzero entry of ``x``; the
result keeps the shape and sparsity of ``x`` (structural zeros stay zero
even when p[n-1] != 0).



Parameters:
    p: Dense column vector of coefficients, at least one entry
    x: Point(s) of evaluation, any shape



::

  >>> polyval(DM([1, 2, 3]), 2)
  DM(11)
  >>> polyval(DM([1, 0, -1]), DM([0, 1, 2]))
  DM([-1, 0, 3])
  >>> polyval(SX.sym(\"p\", 3), SX.sym(\"x\"))
  SX(((((p_0*x)+p_1)*x)+p_2))
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1cc

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1639
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1639-L1641
";

