%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::diag(const MatType &A) "

Get the diagonal of a matrix or construct a diagonal.

If the input is a vector (row or column), a square matrix with the vector on
its diagonal and structural zeros elsewhere is constructed. Otherwise the
diagonal entries are returned as a column vector of length min(size1(),
size2()); only structurally nonzero entries are kept.



::

  >>> diag(DM([1, 2]))
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [00, 2]])
  >>> diag(DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]))
  DM([1, 4])
  >>> diag(DM(Sparsity.upper(2), [1, 2, 3]))
  DM([1, 3])
  >>> diag(DM.ones(2, 3))
  DM([1, 1])
  





See also: trace, diagcat, Sparsity::diag

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1cd

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1678
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1678-L1680
";

