%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::project(const MatType
&A, const Sparsity &sp, bool intersect=false) "

Create a new matrix with a given sparsity pattern but with the.

nonzeros taken from an existing matrix

Entries of ``A`` outside ``sp`` are dropped; entries of ``sp`` not present
in ``A`` become numerical zeros. The shape of ``sp`` must equal that of
``A``. With ``intersect`` true, the target pattern is the intersection of
``sp`` and the pattern of ``A``, so the result only ever loses entries.



::

  >>> project(DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]), Sparsity.diag(2))
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [00, 4]])
  >>> project(DM.eye(2), Sparsity.dense(2, 2))
  DM(
  [[1, 0],
   [0, 1]])
  >>> project(DM(Sparsity.diag(2), [1, 2]), Sparsity.upper(2), True)
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [00, 2]])
  





See also: densify, sparsify, unite

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1ch

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1802
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1802-L1805
";

