https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1855
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1855-L1858
";

%feature("docstring") casadi::casadi_if_else "

Branching on MX nodes.

Ternary operator, \"cond ? if_true : if_false\"

Selects ``if_true`` where ``cond`` is nonzero and ``if_false`` elsewhere.
``cond`` may be a scalar or have the shape of the branches (elementwise
selection); a scalar branch is broadcast. By default the result is
if_else_zero(cond, if_true) + if_else_zero(!cond, if_false): both branches
are part of the expression and are evaluated, but the value of the
unselected branch is discarded, so a nan or inf there does not propagate.
With ``short_circuit`` true (MX only; ignored for SX and DM) the branches
are wrapped in functions and only the selected one is evaluated.



::

  >>> if_else(DM(1), DM(10), DM(20)), if_else(DM(0), DM(10), DM(20))
  (DM(10), DM(20))
  >>> if_else(DM([1, 0]), DM([1, 2]), DM([3, 4]))
  DM([1, 4])
  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> if_else(x > 0, x, -x)
  SX(@1=(0<x), ((@1?x:0)+((!@1)?(-x):0)))
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x], [if_else(x >= 0, sqrt(x), 0)])
  >>> f(-1)
  DM(0)
  >>> X = MX.sym(\"X\")
  >>> if_else(X > 0, X, -X, True)
  MX(switch((0<X), X){0})
  





See also: conditional, if_else_zero, Function::if_else

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1ci

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1855
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L1855-L1858
";

