%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::substitute(const MatType
&ex, const MatType &v, const MatType &vdef) "

Substitute variable v with expression vdef in an expression ex.

``v`` must be symbolic and have the same shape as ``vdef`` (for SX also the
same sparsity). For MX, ``v`` must be a symbolic primitive as created by
MX.sym; an element of such a primitive is rejected. Substituting a symbol
that does not occur in ``ex`` is a no-op. Not defined for DM.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\"); z = SX.sym(\"z\")
  >>> substitute(x*y + x, x, 2)
  SX(((2.*y)+2))
  >>> substitute(x*y + x, x, z**2)
  SX(@1=sq(z), ((@1*y)+@1))
  >>> p = SX.sym(\"p\", 2)
  >>> substitute(sumsqr(p), p, DM([1, 2]))
  SX(5)
  >>> X = MX.sym(\"X\"); Y = MX.sym(\"Y\")
  >>> substitute(X*Y + X, X, Y)
  MX((sq(Y)+Y))
  





See also: substitute_inplace, graph_substitute, Function

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1cl

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2042
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2042-L2045
";

