%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::substitute_inplace(const
std::vector< MatType > &v, std::vector< MatType > &inout_vdef, std::vector<
MatType > &inout_ex, bool reverse=false) "

Inplace substitution with piggyback expressions.

Substitute variables ``v`` out of the expressions ``vdef`` sequentially, as
well as out of a number of other expressions piggyback

Interprets vdef[k] as the definition of the symbol v[k] and resolves the
definitions into each other, so that afterwards neither ``vdef`` nor ``ex``
contain any of the symbols ``v``. Both ``vdef`` and ``ex`` are modified in
place (and returned, in Python). ``v`` must consist of symbolic primitives
with the shapes of ``vdef``. ``reverse`` is only accepted for SX; MX raises
\"Not implemented\".



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> substitute_inplace([x, y], [y + 1, 3], [x*y])
  ([SX(4), SX(3)], [SX(12)])
  >>> X = MX.sym(\"X\"); Y = MX.sym(\"Y\")
  >>> substitute_inplace([X, Y], [Y + 1, 3], [X*Y])
  ([MX(1), MX(3)], [MX(00)])
  





See also: substitute

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1cn

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2117
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2117-L2121
";

