%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::solve(const MatType &A,
const MatType &b, const std::string &lsolver, const Dict &dict=Dict()) "

Solve a system of equations: A*x = b, using a linear solver plugin.

Available for DM and MX (for MX the solve becomes a call to the solver,
evaluated numerically); SX raises an error. A scalar ``A`` gives the
elementwise division b/A.



Parameters:
    lsolver: Name of a Linsol plugin, e.g. \"qr\", \"csparse\", \"lapacklu\", \"lapackqr\", \"symbolicqr\", \"ldl\", \"ma27\"; which ones are available depends on the build
    dict: Options passed to the linear solver



::

  >>> A = DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]])
  >>> solve(A, DM([1, 2]), \"qr\")
  DM([0, 0.5])
  >>> solve(MX.sym(\"A\", 2, 2), MX.sym(\"b\", 2), \"qr\")
  MX((A\\\\b))
  





See also: Linsol, has_linsol

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1cr

