%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::pinv(const MatType &A) "

Computes the Moore-Penrose pseudo-inverse.

If the matrix A is fat (size1<size2), mul(A, pinv(A)) is unity.

pinv(A)' = (AA')^(-1) A

If the matrix A is slender (size1>size2), mul(pinv(A), A) is unity.

pinv(A) = (A'A)^(-1) A'

The normal equations are solved with solve, so ``A`` is assumed to have full
rank. For a square matrix this is the inverse.



::

  >>> A = DM([[1, 0, 0], [0, 2, 0]])
  >>> pinv(A)
  DM(
  [[1, 0],
   [0, 0.5],
   [0, 0]])
  >>> mtimes(A, pinv(A))
  DM(
  [[1, 0],
   [0, 1]])
  >>> pinv(SX.sym(\"A\", 1, 2))
  SX(@1=(sq(A_0)+sq(A_1)), [(A_0/@1), (A_1/@1)])
  





See also: inv, solve, nullspace

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1ct

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2359
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2359-L2361
";

