%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::jacobian(const MatType
&ex, const MatType &arg, const Dict &opts=Dict()) "

Calculate Jacobian.

The derivative of ``ex`` with respect to ``arg``, with both treated as
column-major vectors of their elements: the result is ex.numel()-by-
arg.numel(), one row per element of ``ex`` and one column per element of
``arg``. Entries that are structurally zero are left out of the sparsity
pattern.

``arg`` must be symbolic (for MX: symbolic primitives as created by MX.sym,
or a concatenation of them; elements of a primitive are rejected). Not
defined for DM.



Parameters:
    opts: Options: \"allow_forward\" and \"allow_reverse\" (bool, default true) restrict the AD mode; \"symmetric\" (bool, default false) hints that the Jacobian is symmetric; \"verbose\"



Returns:
    Sparse matrix



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> J = jacobian(vertcat(x*y, x**2), vertcat(x, y))
  >>> J
  SX(
  [[y, x],
   [(2.*x), 00]])
  >>> J.dim(True)
  '2x2,3nz'
  >>> A = SX.sym(\"A\", 2, 2)
  >>> jacobian(2*A, A).dim()
  '4x4'
  >>> jacobian(SX(0, 1), vertcat(x, y)).dim()
  '0x2'
  





See also: gradient, hessian, jtimes, jacobian_sparsity, Function::jacobian

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1cv

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2469
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2469-L2472
";

