%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::forward(const
std::vector< MatType > &ex, const std::vector< MatType > &arg, const
std::vector< std::vector< MatType > > &v, const Dict &opts=Dict()) "

Forward directional derivative.

For each seed direction v[d] (a list with one seed per entry of ``arg``,
with matching shapes), computes the forward sensitivities of every entry of
``ex:`` the result is a list over directions of lists over ``ex``,
containing jtimes(ex[i], arg, v[d]) summed over all arguments. Not defined
for DM.



Parameters:
    ex: List of expressions
    arg: List of symbolic expressions
    v: List of directions, each a list of seeds matching ``arg``
    opts: Options, see jacobian



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> forward([x*y, x**2], [x, y], [[1, 0]])
  [[SX(y), SX((2.*x))]]
  >>> forward([x*y, x**2], [x, y], [[1, 0], [0, 1]])
  [[SX(y), SX((2.*x))], [SX(x), SX(0)]]
  





See also: reverse, jtimes, Function::forward

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1cx

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2627
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2627-L2631
";

