%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::which_depends(const
MatType &expr, const MatType &var, casadi_int order, bool tr) "

Find out which variables enter with some order.

Structural dependency check by sparsity propagation, without forming
derivatives. With ``order`` 1, an entry depends if the corresponding
Jacobian entry is structurally nonzero; with ``order`` 2, if it enters
nonlinearly (second derivative structurally nonzero). Operations whose
derivative is structurally zero, such as floor or sign, count as not
depending.



Parameters:
    expr: Expression
    var: Symbolic expression
    order: 1 or 2; other values raise an error
    tr: When false, the result has one entry per element of ``var:`` does any element of ``expr`` depend on it. When true, one entry per element of ``expr:`` does it depend on any element of ``var``.



Returns:
    List of booleans



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> e = vertcat(x*y, x**2, 3*x)
  >>> which_depends(e, vertcat(x, y), 1, False)
  [True, True]
  >>> which_depends(e, vertcat(x, y), 1, True)
  [True, True, True]
  >>> which_depends(e, vertcat(x, y), 2, True)
  [True, True, False]
  





See also: depends_on, is_linear, jacobian_sparsity

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1cz

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2761
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L2761-L2764
";

