https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L3010-L3016
";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::separate_linear(const
MatType &expr, const MatType &sym_lin, const MatType &sym_const, MatType
&expr_const, MatType &expr_lin, MatType &expr_nonlin) "

Separate an expression into subexpressions that are constant, linear and
nonlinear.



Parameters:
    expr[in]: The expression to be separated
    sym_lin[in]: The symbolic variables w.r.t. which linearity should be checked
    sym_const[in]: The symbolic variables that are deemed constant
    expr_const[out]: The constant part of the expression
    expr_lin[out]: The linear part of the expression
    expr_nonlin[out]: The nonlinear part of the expression

Every symbol in ``expr`` must be listed in ``sym_lin`` or ``sym_const``;
otherwise an error about free variables is raised.

A post condition is that the following holds: expr = expr_const + expr_lin +
expr_nonlin

Here, expr_const is only dependant on sym_const, expr_lin is linear in
sym_lin (with coefficients that may depend on sym_const)

Example:

[expr_const,expr_lin,expr_nonlin] = separate_linear(cos(p)+7*x+x*y,
vertcat(x,y), p)

expr_const: cos(p) expr_lin: 7*x expr_nonlin: x*y

``sym_lin`` and ``sym_const`` may also be lists of symbols. Not defined for
DM.



::

  * >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\"); p = SX.sym(\"p\")
  * >>> separate_linear(cos(p) + 7*x + x*y, vertcat(x, y), p)
  * (SX(cos(p)), SX((7*x)), SX((x*y)))
  * >>> separate_linear(p*x, x, p)
  * (SX(0), SX((p*x)), SX(0))
  * 





See also: extract_parametric, linear_coeff

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2mo

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L3116
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L3116-L3120
";

