%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::n_nodes(const MatType
&A) "

Count the number of nodes in an expression graph.

The number of nodes of the Function that evaluates the expression, which for
SX includes symbols and constants and for MX also output nodes. Shared
subexpressions are counted once; identical subexpressions built separately
are counted separately (use cse to merge them). Not defined for DM.



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> n_nodes(x), n_nodes(x + y), n_nodes(vertcat(x + y, x + y))
  (1, 3, 4)
  >>> n_nodes(SX(0, 1))
  0
  





See also: cse, Function::n_nodes

