%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::set(const Matrix< double >
&m, bool ind1, const Slice &rr, const Slice &cc) "

Assign a submatrix by row and column indices.

Backs the Python statement x[i, j] = v. The matrix is modified in place.
``m`` must be len(rr)-by-len(cc), a scalar (broadcast to all selected
entries) or a vector of the transposed orientation (transposed
automatically); other shapes raise an error. Assigning into structural zeros
inserts nonzeros; assigning a sparse ``m`` first erases the selected block,
so its structural zeros become structural zeros.



Parameters:
    m: Value(s) to assign
    ind1: True for one-based indices (MATLAB); Python always passes false
    rr: Row index, Slice or list/matrix of row indices
    cc: Column index, Slice or list/matrix of column indices



::

  >>> A = DM([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]])
  >>> A[0, 1] = 9; A[1, :] = 0
  >>> A
  DM(
  [[1, 9, 3],
   [0, 0, 0]])
  >>> A[0, :] = DM([7, 8, 9])
  >>> A[0, :]
  DM([[7, 8, 9]])
  >>> A[:, 0] = DM(2, 1)
  >>> A.nnz()
  4
  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\", 2, 2)
  >>> x[0, 0] = 0
  >>> x
  SX(
  [[0, x_2],
   [x_1, x_3]])
  >>> try: A[0, :] = [1, 2]
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  





See also: get

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2ou

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L703
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_impl.hpp#L195-L211
";

