%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::set_nz(const Matrix< double
> &m, bool ind1, const Slice &k) "

Assign structural nonzeros by their position in the nonzero storage.

Backs the Python statement x.nz[k] = v. The sparsity pattern never changes:
only stored values are overwritten (writing 0 keeps the entry as a
structural nonzero). ``m`` must be a scalar (assigned to every selected
nonzero) or have as many entries as there are indices; a mismatch raises an
error.



Parameters:
    m: Value(s) to assign
    ind1: True for one-based indices (MATLAB); Python always passes false
    k: Nonzero index, Slice or list/matrix of indices



::

  >>> S = DM(Sparsity.diag(3))
  >>> S.nz[:] = [4, 5, 6]; S.nz[0] = 0
  >>> S
  DM(
  [[0, 00, 00],
   [00, 5, 00],
   [00, 00, 6]])
  >>> S.nnz()
  3
  >>> try: S.nz[[0, 1]] = [1, 2, 3]
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  





See also: get_nz, set

