%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::expand(const Matrix< double
> &ex, Matrix< double > &weights, Matrix< double > &terms) "

Expand a scalar SX expression as a weighted sum of terms with constant
weights.

Collects additions, subtractions and multiplications by constants so that ex
== dot(weights, terms), merging repeated terms. Any other operation (a
product of two non-constant factors, a function call, ...) is kept as a
single term with weight 1. The input must be a scalar SX; DM is not
supported.



Returns:
    weights and terms, both column vectors (a tuple in Python)



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> w, t = expand(3*x - x + 5*y)
  >>> w, t
  (SX([2, 5]), SX([x, y]))
  >>> w, t = expand(3*(x + y) + 1)
  >>> t
  SX([x, y, 1])
  





See also: linear_coeff

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_192

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1574
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1574-L1577
";

