%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::pw_lin(const Matrix< double
> &t, const Matrix< double > &tval, const Matrix< double > &val) "

Piecewise linear function of a scalar symbolic variable.

Builds an SX expression that interpolates linearly between the points
(tval[k], val[k]). Outside [tval[0], tval[N-1]] the first and last segments
are extrapolated. Only defined for SX.



Parameters:
    t: Scalar SX variable (e.g. time)
    tval: Breakpoints, increasing, at least two
    val: Function values at the breakpoints, same length as ``tval``



::

  >>> t = SX.sym(\"t\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [t], [pw_lin(t, [0, 1, 3], [0, 2, 1])])
  >>> [float(f(v)) for v in [-1, 0, 0.5, 1, 2, 3, 4]]
  [-2.0, 0.0, 1.0, 2.0, 1.5, 1.0, 0.5]
  >>> try: pw_lin(t, [0], [7])
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  





See also: pw_const, interpolant

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_194

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1654
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1654-L1657
";

