Expands ``ex`` around ``a`` with respect to the scalar symbol ``x`` up to
the given order: ex(a) + ex'(a)*(x-a) + ex''(a)*(x-a)^2/2! + ... +
ex^(order)(a)*(x-a)^order/order! The expansion is done entrywise for a dense
matrix ``ex``; sparse ``ex`` raises an error. ``a`` may itself be symbolic.
The two-argument form expands around 0 to first order. Only defined for SX.



Parameters:
