%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::mtaylor(const Matrix<
double > &ex, const Matrix< double > &x, const Matrix< double > &a,
casadi_int order=1) "

Multivariate Taylor series expansion.

Expands ``ex`` around the point ``a`` with respect to the symbols in ``x``,
keeping all terms whose total degree is at most ``order``. The total degree
of x^n*y^m is n+m. ``ex`` and ``x`` must be dense; ``a`` must have the same
number of entries as ``x``. Only defined for SX.



Parameters:
    ex: Dense SX expression to expand
    x: Vector of SX symbols
    a: Expansion point, a vector of the same length as ``x``
    order: Maximum total degree, default 1 (linearization)



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\"); a = SX.sym(\"a\"); b = SX.sym(\"b\")
  >>> mtaylor(sin(x + y), vertcat(x, y), vertcat(a, b), 1)
  SX(((sin((a+b))+(cos((a+b))*(x-a)))+(cos((a+b))*(y-b))))
  >>> mtaylor(exp(x * y), vertcat(x, y), DM([0, 0]), 2)
  SX(@1=2, ((1+((x*y)/@1))+((y*x)/@1)))
  





See also: taylor

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_23r

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1879
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1879-L1882
";

