%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::poly_roots(const Matrix<
double > &p) "

Roots of a polynomial given by its coefficients, in closed form.

``p`` is a dense column vector of coefficients in decreasing power order, as
returned by poly_coeff. Closed-form formulas are used for degrees 1 to 4; a
zero constant term is split off as a root 0 first. Higher degrees raise an
error. All roots are assumed real: complex roots give nan. The result stays
symbolic for symbolic coefficients. Only defined for SX; pass SX(p) for
numeric coefficients.



::

  >>> poly_roots(SX([1, -3, 2]))
  SX([1, 2])
  >>> evalf(poly_roots(SX([1, -6, 11, -6])))
  DM([3, 1, 2])
  >>> a = SX.sym(\"a\")
  >>> poly_roots(vertcat(a, 2))
  SX((-2/a))
  >>> try: poly_roots(SX([1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]))
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  





See also: poly_coeff, eig_symbolic

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_198

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1986
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1986-L1988
";

