%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::eig_symbolic(const Matrix<
double > &m) "

Eigenvalues of a square SX matrix in closed form.

Splits the matrix into its strongly connected (block diagonal) components
and solves the characteristic polynomial of each block with poly_roots, so
every block may be at most 4-by-4. Larger blocks raise an error. Eigenvalues
are assumed real. Returns a column vector; the order follows the block
structure, not the magnitude. Only defined for SX; pass SX(m) for a numeric
matrix.



::

  >>> evalf(eig_symbolic(SX([[2, 1], [1, 2]])))
  DM([1, 3])
  >>> M = SX.sym(\"M\", 2, 2)
  >>> eig_symbolic(M)
  SX(@1=(M_3+M_0), @2=sqrt((sq(@1)-(4*((M_0*M_3)-(M_2*M_1))))), @3=2, [((@1-@2)/@3),
  ((@1+@2)/@3)])
  >>> evalf(eig_symbolic(SX.eye(5) * 3)).T
  DM([[3, 3, 3, 3, 3]])
  





See also: poly_roots, Sparsity::scc

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_199

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L2022
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L2022-L2024
";

