triangle of A is referenced. The sparsity pattern of A must be symmetric.
Only guaranteed to work for positive definite matrices (no pivoting). Works
symbolically on SX.



Parameters:
    A: Square matrix with symmetric sparsity pattern
    amd: Use an approximate minimum degree ordering to reduce fill-in



Returns:
    D, LT, p (a tuple in Python)



::

  >>> D, LT, p = ldl(DM([[4, 2], [2, 3]]))
  >>> D, p
  (DM([4, 2]), [0, 1])
  >>> LT
  DM(
  [[00, 0.5],
   [00, 00]])
  >>> L = DM.eye(2) + LT.T
  >>> mtimes(mtimes(L, diag(D)), L.T)
  DM(
  [[4, 2],
   [2, 3]])
  





See also: ldl_solve, chol, Sparsity::ldl

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_18w

