%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::adj(const Matrix< double >
&A) "

Adjugate (classical adjoint) of a square matrix.

Transpose of the cofactor matrix, computed by Laplace expansion. For an
invertible matrix inv(A) == adj(A)/det(A). Cost grows factorially with the
size; intended for small (symbolic) matrices. A structural zero cofactor
stays structurally zero. A non-square input raises an error.



::

  >>> adj(DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]))
  DM(
  [[4, -2],
   [-3, 1]])
  >>> X = SX.sym(\"X\", 2, 2)
  >>> adj(X)
  SX(
  [[X_3, (-X_2)],
   [(-X_1), X_0]])
  >>> adj(DM(5)), adj(DM(Sparsity.diag(3))).nnz()
  (DM(1), 3)
  





See also: inv_minor, cofactor, det

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_18p

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1121
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1121-L1123
";

