%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::minor(const Matrix< double
> &x, casadi_int i, casadi_int j) "

Minor of a square matrix: determinant with one column and one row removed.

Note the argument order: ``i`` is the column that is removed, ``j`` the row.
The input must be square; a 1-by-1 input gives 1.



Parameters:
    x: Square matrix
    i: Column index to remove (zero-based)
    j: Row index to remove (zero-based)



::

  >>> A = DM([[1, 2, 3], [0, 1, 4], [5, 6, 0]])
  >>> minor(A, 0, 1)
  DM(-18)
  >>> X = SX.sym(\"X\", 2, 2)
  >>> minor(X, 0, 1)
  SX(X_2)
  





See also: cofactor, adj, det

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_18q

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1155
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1155-L1157
";

