%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::chol(const Matrix< double >
&A) "

Cholesky factorization of a symmetric positive definite matrix.

Returns the upper triangular factor R with R^T*R == A, obtained from the
sparse LDL^T factorization (without fill-reducing permutation) as
diag(sqrt(D))*L^T. The sparsity pattern of A must be symmetric; otherwise an
error is raised. An indefinite A gives nan entries without an error. Works
symbolically on SX.



::

  >>> R = chol(DM([[4, 2], [2, 3]]))
  >>> R
  DM(
  [[2, 1],
   [00, 1.41421]])
  >>> mtimes(R.T, R)
  DM(
  [[4, 2],
   [2, 3]])
  >>> chol(DM(Sparsity.diag(3)) * 4).nnz()
  3
  





See also: ldl, qr

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_18v

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1346
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L1346-L1348
";

