%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::triplet(const std::vector<
casadi_int > &row, const std::vector< casadi_int > &col, const Matrix<
double > &d) "

Construct a sparse matrix from triplet form (row indices, column indices,
values)

Entry k of the result is at (row[k], col[k]) with value d[k]. The three
lists must have the same length; indices are zero-based and must be within
the matrix bounds. The nonzeros are reordered into column- major order. When
the same (row, col) pair appears more than once, only the first value is
kept; duplicates are not summed.



Parameters:
    row: Row index of each entry
    col: Column index of each entry
    d: Dense vector of values, one per entry
    nrow: Number of rows of the result
    ncol: Number of columns of the result



::

  >>> DM.triplet([0, 1], [1, 0], [5, 6], 3, 3)
  DM(
  [[00, 5, 00],
   [6, 00, 00],
   [00, 00, 00]])
  >>> DM.triplet([0, 1], [1, 0], [5, 6], (3, 3)).nonzeros()
  [6.0, 5.0]
  >>> SX.triplet([0, 1], [0, 1], SX.sym(\"v\", 2), 2, 2)
  SX(
  [[v_0, 00],
   [00, v_1]])
  >>> DM.triplet([], [], [], 2, 2).nnz()
  0
  >>> try: DM.triplet([0, 1], [1, 0], [5], 3, 3)
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  





See also: Sparsity::triplet

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_23t

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L2571
";

