%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::Matrix(casadi_int nrow,
casadi_int ncol) "

Create a matrix of the given shape with all structural zeros (no nonzeros)

The result has nnz()==0. Use zeros(nrow, ncol) for a dense matrix of
numerical zeros. Structural zeros print as 00.



Parameters:
    nrow: Number of rows, nonnegative
    ncol: Number of columns, nonnegative



::

  >>> DM(2, 3)
  DM(
  [[00, 00, 00],
   [00, 00, 00]])
  >>> DM(2, 3).nnz(), DM.zeros(2, 3).nnz()
  (0, 6)
  >>> SX(2, 0).dim()
  '2x0'
  





See also: zeros, ones

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_18g

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L187
";

