%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::Matrix(const Sparsity &sp,
const Matrix< double > &d) "

Create a matrix with a given sparsity pattern and given nonzeros.



Parameters:
    sp: Sparsity pattern of the result
    d: Either a scalar, which is used for every structural nonzero, or a dense vector (row or column) with exactly sp.nnz() entries, in column-major order of the pattern. Anything else raises an error.



::

  >>> DM(Sparsity.diag(2), [5, 6])
  DM(
  [[5, 00],
   [00, 6]])
  >>> DM(Sparsity.diag(2), 5)
  DM(
  [[5, 00],
   [00, 5]])
  >>> SX(Sparsity.lower(2), SX.sym(\"v\", 3))
  SX(
  [[v_0, 00],
   [v_1, v_2]])
  >>> try: DM(Sparsity.diag(3), [1, 2])
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_18l

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L266
";

