%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::Matrix(const std::vector<
std::vector< double > > &m) "

Dense matrix from a list of rows.

Every row must have the same length; a ragged input raises an error. An
empty outer list gives a 0-by-1 matrix. At the Python level, 2-D NumPy
arrays and SciPy sparse matrices are accepted as well; a sparse input keeps
its sparsity pattern.



::

  >>> DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]])
  DM(
  [[1, 2],
   [3, 4]])
  >>> DM(np.array([[1, 2], [3, 4]])).dim()
  '2x2'
  >>> try: DM([[1, 2], [3]])
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2oo

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L292
";

