%feature("docstring") casadi::Matrix< double >::Matrix(const Matrix< A > &x)
"

Create a matrix from another matrix with a different entry type.

The sparsity pattern is kept and every nonzero is converted. SX(DM) always
works. DM(SX) requires constant entries: a symbolic entry is converted to
nan without an error. Use evalf to get an error instead.



::

  >>> SX(DM(Sparsity.diag(2))).dim()
  '2x2'
  >>> DM(SX([1, 2]))
  DM([1, 2])
  >>> DM(SX.sym(\"x\"))
  DM(nan)
  





See also: evalf

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_18n

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L340
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L340-L343
";

