%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::has_nz(casadi_int rr,
casadi_int cc) const "

Check whether element (rr, cc) is a structural nonzero.

Looks only at the sparsity pattern; a stored numerical zero still counts as
a nonzero. Negative indices count from the end. An index past the end raises
an error.



::

  >>> S = DM(Sparsity.diag(2))
  >>> S.has_nz(0, 0), S.has_nz(0, 1), DM([0, 1]).has_nz(0, 0)
  (True, False, True)
  





See also: has_zeros, Sparsity::has_nz

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2op

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L411
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_impl.hpp#L75-L77
";

