%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::print_split(std::vector<
std::string > &nz, std::vector< std::string > &inter) const "

String representation of each nonzero and of the shared subexpressions.

Returns two lists: one string per nonzero (in storage order) and the
definitions of the intermediate expressions \"@1\", \"@2\", ... that the
nonzero strings refer to (always empty for DM).



::

  >>> DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]).print_split()
  (['1', '3', '2', '4'], [])
  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); y = SX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> e = x * y
  >>> vertcat(e + 1, e - 1).print_split()
  (['(@1+@2)', '(@1-@2)'], ['(x*y)', '1'])
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2oy

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L2199
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_impl.hpp#L701-L705
";

