%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::resize(casadi_int nrow,
casadi_int ncol) "

Change the shape in place, keeping nonzeros that remain inside the new
bounds.

Growing appends structural zeros; shrinking drops the entries outside the
new shape.



::

  >>> A = DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]])
  >>> A.resize(3, 3)
  >>> A
  DM(
  [[1, 2, 00],
   [3, 4, 00],
   [00, 00, 00]])
  >>> A.resize(1, 1)
  >>> A
  DM(1)
  





See also: enlarge, reshape

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2p4

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L2342
";

