%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::erase(const std::vector<
casadi_int > &rr, const std::vector< casadi_int > &cc, bool ind1=false) "

Erase the block at the given rows and columns, leaving structural zeros.

The shape is unchanged; the entries of the submatrix rr x cc are removed
from the sparsity pattern. Negative indices count from the end; out-of-range
indices raise an error.



Parameters:
    rr: Row indices
    cc: Column indices
    ind1: True for one-based indices



::

  >>> A = DM([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]])
  >>> A.erase([0], [1])
  >>> A
  DM(
  [[1, 00, 3],
   [4, 5, 6]])
  >>> A.dim(), A.nnz()
  ('2x3', 5)
  





See also: remove, sparsify

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_19f

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L2382
";

