%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::is_regular() const "

Check that no entry is nan, inf or -inf.

Structural zeros are ignored. For SX, every entry must be a constant: the
check raises an error when it reaches a symbolic entry (an infinite constant
found before it still gives false).



::

  >>> DM([1, 2]).is_regular(), DM([1, inf]).is_regular(), DM.nan(2, 2).is_regular()
  (True, False, False)
  >>> DM(2, 2).is_regular(), SX([1, 2]).is_regular()
  (True, True)
  >>> try: SX.sym(\"x\").is_regular()
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"error\")
  error
  





See also: nan, inf

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2p5

