%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::is_symbolic() const "

Check if symbolic (Dense)

Check if an expression is a pure symbol. Pure means that no operations
should happen on the symbol (not even vec, transpose, index, concatenation,
...) By consequence, a slice of a vector-shaped MX symbol is not a symbol.
However, the SX type is really a container format with scalar entries.
Therefore, a slice of a vector-shaped SX symbol is still a symbol.

Sparse matrices invariable return false

\\\\seealso is_valid_input

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_19r

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L2775
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sx_instantiator.cpp#L182-L188
";

