%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::to_file(const std::string
&filename, const std::string &format="") const "

Write a numerical matrix to a text file (DM only)

Supported formats, selected by the file extension unless ``format`` is
given:

- mtx: Matrix Market coordinate format (sparse, one-based row/col/value triplets)
- txt: one line per row, whitespace separated, aligned columns, full precision, structural zeros written as 00. Does not scale to large sparse matrices. Values are written with the C locale; nan and inf round-trip. An unknown extension or format raises an error. SX is not supported.





Parameters:
    filename: Output path
    format: \"mtx\" or \"txt\"; empty means deduce from the extension



::

  >>> import os, tempfile
  >>> fn = os.path.join(tempfile.mkdtemp(), \"a.txt\")
  >>> A = DM(Sparsity.diag(2)) * 2.5
  >>> A.to_file(fn)
  >>> DM.from_file(fn)
  DM(
  [[2.5, 00],
   [00, 2.5]])
  >>> os.remove(fn); os.rmdir(os.path.dirname(fn))
  





See also: from_file, Sparsity::to_file

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2p9

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L3354
";

