%feature("docstring")  casadi::Matrix< double >::from_file(const std::string
&filename, const std::string &format_hint="") "

Read a numerical matrix from a text file written by to_file (DM only)

Same formats as to_file. In txt format, lines starting with #, % or / and
empty lines are skipped, 00 marks a structural zero and a plain 0 a stored
zero; every row must have the same number of columns, otherwise an error is
raised. An empty file gives a 0-by-0 matrix. A missing file raises an error.



Parameters:
    filename: Input path
    format_hint: \"mtx\" or \"txt\"; empty means deduce from the extension



::

  >>> import os, tempfile
  >>> fn = os.path.join(tempfile.mkdtemp(), \"a.txt\")
  >>> with open(fn, \"w\") as f: n = f.write(\"# comment\\\\n1 00\\\\n0 2\\\\n\")
  >>> A = DM.from_file(fn)
  >>> A
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [0, 2]])
  >>> A.nnz()
  3
  >>> os.remove(fn); os.rmdir(os.path.dirname(fn))
  





See also: to_file

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2pa

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/matrix_decl.hpp#L3399
";

