of ``x`` whose value is not zero, or to the length of ``x`` when all entries
are zero. Structural zeros are skipped. The result is piecewise constant, so
its derivative is zero. ``x`` must be a column or row vector; matrices raise
an error.



::

  >>> v = MX.sym(\"v\", 3)
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [v], [find(v)])
  >>> find(v).shape, f(DM([0, 3, 1])), f(DM([0, 0, 0]))
  ((1, 1), DM(1), DM(3))
  >>> evalf(find(MX(DM(Sparsity.unit(3, 2), [1]))))
  DM(2)
  >>> try:
  ...   find(MX.sym(\"A\", 2, 2))
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Argument must be vector\" in str(e))
  True
  





