%feature("docstring")  casadi::MX::graph_substitute(const MX &ex, const
std::vector< MX > &v, const std::vector< MX > &vdef) "

Substitute nodes in the expression graph, by node identity.

Replaces every occurrence of the node v[i] in ``ex`` by vdef[i]. Unlike
substitute, which only accepts symbolic primitives for ``v``,
graph_substitute matches any node, so intermediate results and Function call
results can be replaced. Matching is by identity: an expression that was
rebuilt (x + y created twice) is a different node and is not matched. Nodes
that do not depend on any substituted node are reused, not copied. Shapes of
v[i] and vdef[i] must agree.



Parameters:
    ex: Expression to substitute in
    v: Nodes to replace
    vdef: Replacements, same length as ``v``
    updated: Set to true if any substitution took place (C++ only)



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> y = MX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> s = x + y
  >>> e = sin(s) + s
  >>> graph_substitute(e, [s], [MX(3)])
  MX(3.14112)
  >>> graph_substitute(e, [x + y], [MX(3)])
  MX(@1=(x+y), (sin(@1)+@1))
  >>> try:
  ...   substitute(e, s, MX(3))
  ... except Exception as err:
  ...   print(\"not symbolic\" in str(err))
  True
  >>> try:
  ...   graph_substitute(e, [s], [MX.sym(\"z\", 2)])
  ... except Exception as err:
  ...   print(\"Inconsistent shapes\" in str(err))
  True
  





See also: substitute

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_r9

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/mx.hpp#L2769
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/mx.hpp#L2769-L2772 ";

