%feature("docstring")  casadi::MX::matrix_expand(const MX &e, const
std::vector< MX > &boundary=std::vector< MX >(), const Dict &options=Dict())
"

Expand an MX expression into a call to an SX Function.

Converts the whole matrix graph of ``e`` to scalar SX operations (including
inlined Function calls, as Function.expand does) and returns a call to the
resulting SXFunction, with the free symbols of ``e`` as arguments.
Expressions listed in ``boundary`` are not expanded: they stay as MX inputs
of the call.



Parameters:
    e: Expression to expand
    boundary: Sub-expressions at which the expansion stops
    options: Options for the SXFunction, forwarded to Function.expand



Returns:
    An OutputNode of the SXFunction call



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> g = Function(\"g\", [x], [x**2 + 1])
  >>> sx = sin(x)
  >>> e = g(x) + sx
  >>> r = matrix_expand(e)
  >>> r, r.is_output(), r.dep(0).which_function()
  (MX(expand_tmp_matrix_expand(x){0}), True, Function(expand_tmp_matrix_expand:(i0)->(o0)
  SXFunction))
  >>> Function(\"f\", [x], [r])(2)
  DM(5.9093)
  >>> matrix_expand(e, [sx]).dep(0).which_function()
  Function(expand_tmp_matrix_expand:(i0,i1)->(o0) SXFunction)
  





See also: Function.expand

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_rb

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/mx.hpp#L2865
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/mx.hpp#L2865-L2868 ";

