%feature("docstring")  casadi::MX::bspline(const MX &x, const DM &coeffs,
const std::vector< std::vector< double > > &knots, const std::vector<
casadi_int > &degree, casadi_int m, const Dict &opts=Dict()) "

Evaluate a tensor-product B-spline with fixed coefficients.

Returns an ``m-by-1`` expression with the spline values at ``x``. The spline
is defined by one knot vector and one degree per dimension; the number of
basis functions per dimension is len(knots[i]) - degree[i] - 1 and the
coefficient vector must hold m times the product of these counts, in column-
major order. Outside the knot range the spline is zero. Derivatives are
available.



Parameters:
    x: Column vector with one entry per dimension
    coeffs: Coefficient vector; its length is not validated
    knots: One knot vector per dimension, numeric
    degree: Degree per dimension; must have as many entries as ``knots``
    m: Number of outputs per evaluation
    opts: \"lookup_mode\" (see low) and \"inline\" (bool, default false: build an explicit expression instead of a BSpline node). Unknown keys are ignored.



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> knots = [[0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 2, 3, 3, 3, 3]]
  >>> c = DM(range(6))
  >>> y = bspline(x, c, knots, [3], 1)
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x], [y])
  >>> y, f(1.5), f(4)
  (MX(BSpline(x)), DM(2.5), DM(0))
  >>> Function(\"df\", [x], [jacobian(y, x)])(1.5)
  DM(1.125)
  >>> try:
  ...   bspline(MX.sym(\"v\", 2), c, knots, [3], 1)
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"must match\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: bspline_dual, interpolant

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2qi

