%feature("docstring")  casadi::MX::stop_diff(const MX &expr, casadi_int
order) "

Stop derivatives of an expression with respect to all its symbolic
variables.

Wraps ``expr`` in a non-inlined Function call whose derivatives of the given
order are declared zero. The value is unchanged. With ``order`` 1 the
expression is treated as a constant by all differentiation; with ``order`` 2
first derivatives are propagated normally but second derivatives are zero.
Other orders raise an error.



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> e = x * stop_diff(x**2, 1)
  >>> Function(\"f\", [x], [e, jacobian(e, x)])(3)
  (DM(27), DM(9))
  





See also: no_grad, no_hess

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_25l

