%feature("docstring")  casadi::MX::difference(const std::vector< MX > &a,
const std::vector< MX > &b) "

Return all elements of ``a`` that do not occur in ``b``, preserving order.

Comparison is by node identity, not by value: two separately built
expressions with the same formula are different nodes. Duplicates in ``a``
are kept.



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> y = MX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> difference([x, y, x], [y]), difference([x + 1], [x + 1])
  ([MX(x), MX(x)], [MX((1+x))])
  





