%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericMatrixCommon::bilin(const MX &A, const
MX &x, const MX &y) "

Calculate bilinear/quadratic form x^T A y.

``x`` and ``y`` must be vectors (row vectors are transposed, sparse vectors
densified) with x.numel() == A.size1() and y.numel() == A.size2(); otherwise
an error is raised. The result is scalar. When ``y`` is omitted, the
quadratic form x^T A x is calculated.



::

  >>> A = DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]])
  >>> bilin(A, DM([1, 1]), DM([1, 2]))
  DM(16)
  >>> bilin(A, DM([1, 1]))
  DM(10)
  >>> bilin(MX.sym(\"A\", 2, 2), MX.sym(\"x\", 2), MX.sym(\"y\", 2))
  MX(bilin(A, x, y))
  





See also: rank1, dot, mtimes

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1bo

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_matrix.hpp#L881
";

