%feature("docstring")  casadi::MX::set(const MX &m, bool ind1, const Slice
&rr) "

Assign to a submatrix by linear index (what x[k] = m does)

Expressions are immutable: assignment rebinds this object to a new
SetNonzeros node whose dependencies are the old expression and ``m``.
Expressions built earlier from the old value are unaffected, but a second
name bound to the same object (Y0 = Y) sees the new node; copy the handle
with MX(Y) to keep the old value. The sparsity pattern grows to include the
assigned elements; assigning a sparse ``m`` first erases the targeted
elements. ``m`` must have the shape of the index set, be a scalar
(broadcast), or be its transpose when the index set is a vector; anything
else raises a dimension mismatch error. A Sparsity index assigns to the
nonzero positions of that pattern. An MX index is only supported for the
nonzero (x.nz[k]) form.



::

  >>> Y = MX.sym(\"Y\", 3, 3)
  >>> alias, copy, twice = Y, MX(Y), 2*Y
  >>> Y[[4]] = 5
  >>> Y, Y.n_dep(), Y.dep(0), Y.dep(1)
  (MX((Y[4] = 5)), 2, MX(Y), MX(5))
  >>> alias, copy, twice
  (MX((Y[4] = 5)), MX(Y), MX((2.*Y)))
  >>> Z = MX(3, 3)
  >>> Z[[0, 8]] = MX.sym(\"a\", 2)
  >>> Z.sparsity()
  Sparsity(3x3,2nz)
  >>> Y = MX.sym(\"Y\", 3, 3)
  >>> Y[Sparsity.lower(3)] = 1
  >>> Y
  MX((Y[0, 1, 2, 4, 5, 8] = ones(6x1)))
  





See also: get, set_nz

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2qc

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/mx.hpp#L2127
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/mx.cpp#L315-L318 ";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::MX::set(const MX &m, bool ind1, const Slice
&rr, const Slice &cc) "

Assign to a submatrix by row and column index (what x[i, j] = m does)

Same semantics as the single-index form. ``m`` must be len(rr)-by-len(cc), a
scalar, or the transpose of a vector block.



::

  >>> Y = MX.sym(\"Y\", 3, 3)
  >>> Y[:, 0] = MX.sym(\"c\", 1, 3)
  >>> Y
  MX((Y[:3] = c'))
  >>> Y[0:2, 0:2] = 0
  >>> Y.sparsity()
  Sparsity(3x3)
  >>> try:
  ...   Y[:, 0] = MX.sym(\"d\", 2)
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Dimension mismatch\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: get

