Rebinds this object to a SetNonzeros node; the sparsity pattern is
unchanged. ``m`` must have as many nonzeros as the index set or be a scalar.
With an MX index the assignment is parametric and resolved at evaluation
time.



::

  >>> Y = MX.sym(\"Y\", 3, 3)
  >>> Y.nz[0] = 7
