%feature("docstring")  casadi::MX::interpn_linear(const std::vector< MX >
&x, const MX &v, const std::vector< MX > &xq, const Dict &opts=Dict()) "

Low-level inlined multilinear interpolation.

Builds the interpolation as explicit MX operations (low, nonzero lookups and
arithmetic) instead of an interpolant Function, so that the grid and values
can be symbolic. Usually you want interpolant('name', 'linear', ...)
instead. Extrapolates linearly outside the grid.



Parameters:
    x: Grid points, one vector per dimension
    v: Values on the grid, flattened in column-major order over the grid; its length must be an integer multiple m of the number of grid points, giving m outputs per query point
    xq: Query coordinates, one vector per dimension, all of the same length nq
    opts: \"lookup_mode\": list with one of \"linear\", \"exact\", \"binary\", \"auto\" (default) per dimension, see low



Returns:
    nq-by-m matrix



::

  >>> g = MX.sym(\"g\", 3)
  >>> v = MX.sym(\"v\", 3)
  >>> xq = MX.sym(\"xq\", 2)
  >>> e = MX.interpn_linear([g], v, [xq])
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [g, v, xq], [e])
  >>> f(DM([0, 1, 2]), DM([0, 10, 40]), DM([0.5, 3]))
  DM([5, 70])
  >>> try:
  ...   MX.interpn_linear([g], MX.sym(\"w\", 4), [xq])
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Dimension mismatch\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: interpolant, low

