%feature("docstring") casadi::MX::MX(const Sparsity &sp, const MX &val) "

Construct a matrix with a given sparsity pattern and given nonzeros.



Parameters:
    sp: Sparsity pattern of the result
    val: Either a scalar, which is repeated over all nonzeros of ``sp``, or a column vector with exactly sp.nnz() entries, which become the nonzeros of the result in column-major order. A matrix whose shape is a reshape of ``sp`` is reshaped. Anything else is an error.

``val`` may be symbolic; the result is then an expression, not a constant.



::

  >>> v = MX.sym(\"v\", 3)
  >>> L = MX(Sparsity.lower(2), v)
  >>> L.sparsity(), L.is_constant()
  (Sparsity(2x2,3nz), False)
  >>> Function(\"f\", [v], [L])(DM([1, 2, 3]))
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [2, 3]])
  >>> evalf(MX(Sparsity.lower(2), MX(7)))
  DM(
  [[7, 00],
   [7, 7]])
  





See also: MX.sym, sparsity_cast

