%feature("docstring")  casadi::MX::is_call() const "

Check if the node is a call to a Function.

A call to a Function with several outputs is a single call node; the values
you get back from calling the Function are OutputNodes that reference it
(see is_output). MX Functions are inlined when called with MX arguments
unless never_inline is set, so no call node appears in that case.



::

  >>> a = SX.sym(\"a\")
  >>> f = Function(\"f\", [a], [a + 1, 2*a])
  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> r0, r1 = f(x, )
  >>> r0.is_call(), r0.is_output(), r0.dep(0).is_call()
  (False, True, True)
  >>> r0.dep(0).which_function().name()
