%feature("docstring")  casadi::MX::mapping() const "

Get the nonzero mapping of a GetNonzeros or SetNonzeros node.

For a slicing node (x[...], x.nz[...]) returns the indices of the nonzeros
of the dependency that make up the result; for an assignment node, the
target indices. Any other node raises an error.



::

  >>> X = MX.sym(\"X\", 3, 3)
  >>> X[0, 1].mapping(), X[:, 1].mapping()
  (DM(3), DM([3, 4, 5]))
  >>> try:
  ...   X.mapping()
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"'mapping' not defined\" in str(e))
  True
  





See also: info

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_ri

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/mx.hpp#L3475
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/mx.cpp#L886-L888 ";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::MX::eval_mx(const std::vector< MX > &arg,
std::vector< MX > &res, const std::vector< bool > &unique=std::vector< bool
>()) const "

Re-apply the operation of this node to new dependencies.

Creates the same operation as this node, applied to ``arg`` instead of the
node's own dependencies, with the usual simplifications. ``arg`` must have
exactly n_dep() entries of matching shapes; a mismatch is a developer error.
Symbolic primitives and constants return the node itself. Call nodes are re-
called with the new arguments; OutputNodes cannot be evaluated this way.
Mainly useful for writing graph transformations.



Parameters:
    arg: New dependencies
    unique: Internal hints that the arguments are not referenced elsewhere; leave empty



Returns:
    List with n_out() results



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> y = MX.sym(\"y\")
  >>> (x * y).eval_mx([MX(2), MX(3)]), (x + y).eval_mx([y, x])
  ([MX(6)], [MX((y+x))])
  >>> MX.sym(\"v\", 3)[1].eval_mx([MX([4, 5, 6])])
  [MX([4, 5, 6][1])]
  





See also: dep, n_dep, graph_substitute

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_rn

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/mx.hpp#L3634
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/mx.cpp#L3222-L3230 ";

