%feature("docstring")  casadi::MX::no_grad(const MX &expr) "

Treat an expression as constant for differentiation (stop first derivatives)

Same as stop_diff(expr, 1): the value is unchanged but all derivatives with
respect to the symbols in ``expr`` are zero.



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> y = no_grad(x**2)
  >>> Function(\"f\", [x], [y])(3), jacobian(y, x).nnz()
  (DM(9), 0)
  >>> Function(\"f\", [x], [jacobian(x * y, x)])(3)
  DM(9)
  





See also: stop_diff, no_hess

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_25m

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/mx.hpp#L3236
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/mx.hpp#L3236-L3238 ";

