%feature("docstring")  casadi::MX::no_hess(const MX &expr) "

Stop second derivatives of an expression wrt all its symbolic variables.

Same as stop_diff(expr, 2): first derivatives are exact, the Hessian
contribution is zero. Useful for Gauss-Newton-type Hessians.



::

  >>> x = MX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> y = no_hess(x**3)
  >>> Function(\"f\", [x], [jacobian(y, x)])(2), hessian(y, x)[0].nnz()
