%feature("docstring")  casadi::OptiAdvanced::show_infeasibilities(double
tol=0, const Dict &opts=Dict()) const "

Print the constraints violated at the latest iterate.

For every row of g whose violation max(g-ubg, lbg-g) is at least ``tol``,
prints the bounds, the value, the violation and the description of the
constraint (also in scaled units when scaling is active). Requires a solve;
typically called after an infeasible solve through opti.debug.



Parameters:
    tol: Violation threshold (default 0, which also lists rounding-level violations)
    opts: Passed to g_describe



::

  >>> opti = Opti()
  >>> x = opti.variable()
  >>> opti.minimize(x**2)
  >>> opti.subject_to(x >= 1)
  >>> opti.subject_to(x <= -1)
  >>> opti.solver(\"ipopt\", {\"print_time\": False}, {\"print_level\": 0, \"sb\": \"yes\"})
  >>> try:
  ...   opti.solve()
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   pass
  >>> opti.debug.show_infeasibilities(1e-6)
  Violated constraints (tol 1e-06), in order of declaration:
  ------- i = 0/2 ------
  1 <= ... <= inf (viol ...)
  Opti constraint of shape 1x1, called from ...
  ------- i = 1/2 ------
  -inf <= ... <= -1 (viol ...)
  Opti constraint of shape 1x1, called from ...
  



