%feature("docstring")  casadi::OptiAdvanced::solve_prepare() "

Prepare the solver arguments (first half of solve)

Checks the constraints and parameter values and fills arg() with x0, p,
lam_g0, lbg and ubg. solve_actual() then runs the solver on such a dict, and
res() stores its result so that value() works. Together they allow custom
solver invocations.



::

  >>> opti = Opti()
  >>> x = opti.variable()
  >>> p = opti.parameter()
  >>> opti.minimize((x-p)**2)
  >>> opti.subject_to(x <= 1)
  >>> opti.set_value(p, 3)
  >>> opti.solver(\"ipopt\", {\"print_time\": False}, {\"print_level\": 0, \"sb\": \"yes\"})
  >>> sol = opti.solve()
  >>> d = opti.debug
  >>> d.solve_prepare()
  >>> d.arg()
  {'lam_g0': DM(0), 'lbg': DM(-inf), 'p': DM(3), 'ubg': DM(1), 'x0': DM(0)}
  >>> r = d.solve_actual(d.arg())
  >>> d.res(r)
  >>> round(d.value(x), 4), sorted(d.res().keys())
  (1.0, ['f', 'g', 'lam_g', 'lam_p', 'lam_x', 'x'])
  



