%feature("docstring")  casadi::Opti::solve() "

Solve the problem.

Builds (or reuses) the solver, evaluates the bounds for the current
parameter values, runs the solver from the current initial guess and returns
an OptiSol snapshot. Raises an error when the solver does not report success
(including iteration or time limits, see solve_limited()); the latest
iterate then remains available through opti.debug.value() and opti.value().
Calling solve() again without changing anything repeats the same solve from
the same initial guess.



Returns:
    OptiSol copy of the problem and its solution



::

  >>> opti = Opti()
  >>> x = opti.variable()
  >>> opti.minimize((x-1)**6)
  >>> opti.solver(\"ipopt\", {\"print_time\": False},
  ...             {\"print_level\": 0, \"max_iter\": 2, \"sb\": \"yes\"})
  >>> try:
  ...   opti.solve()
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(\"Solver failed\" in str(e), \"'Maximum_Iterations_Exceeded'\" in str(e))
  True True
  >>> round(opti.debug.value(x), 2), opti.return_status()
  (0.36, 'Maximum_Iterations_Exceeded')
  >>> opti.solver(\"ipopt\", {\"print_time\": False}, {\"print_level\": 0, \"sb\": \"yes\"})
  >>> sol = opti.solve()
  >>> round(sol.value(x), 1), sol.stats()[\"success\"]
  (1.0, True)
  





See also: solve_limited, OptiSol, stats, return_status

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2mu

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/optistack.hpp#L827
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/optistack.cpp#L213-L219
";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::Opti::solve_limited() "

Solve the problem, accepting a limit as outcome.

Same as solve(), but does not raise when the solver stopped because of an
iteration or time limit (unified_return_status \"SOLVER_RET_LIMITED\");
other failures such as infeasibility still raise.



::

  >>> opti = Opti()
  >>> x = opti.variable()
