%feature("docstring")  casadi::Opti::scale_helper(const Function &h) const "

Scale a helper function constructed via opti.x, opti.g, ...

Wraps a user-written derivative function so that it operates in the scaled
space the solver sees (set_linear_scale(), minimize()/subject_to() scales).
``h`` must be named \"nlp_jac_g\" (inputs x, p; outputs g, jac_g_x) or
\"nlp_hess_l\" (inputs x, p, lam_f, lam_g; output the Lagrangian Hessian);
other names raise an error. The result can be handed to a solver that
accepts custom derivative functions.



::

  >>> opti = Opti()
  >>> x = opti.variable()
  >>> p = opti.parameter()
  >>> opti.set_linear_scale(x, 2, 1)
  >>> opti.minimize((x-p)**2)
  >>> opti.subject_to(x >= 0)
  >>> h = Function(\"nlp_jac_g\", [opti.x, opti.p], [opti.g, jacobian(opti.g, opti.x)],
  ...              [\"x\", \"p\"], [\"g\", \"jac_g_x\"])
  >>> hs = opti.scale_helper(h)
  >>> hs(x=3, p=0)
  {'g': DM(7), 'jac_g_x': DM(2)}
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2ci

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/optistack.hpp#L1092
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/optistack.cpp#L254-L260
";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::Opti::dual(const MX &m) const "

Get the dual variable (Lagrange multiplier) of a constraint.

``m`` must be the exact expression object that was passed to subject_to().
The result is symbolic; evaluate it with value(). For inequality constraints
the dual is nonnegative (the sign of lam_g is removed); for equality
constraints it equals the corresponding entries of lam_g. Keep a reference
to the constraint expression when you need its dual later.



::

  >>> opti = Opti()
  >>> x = opti.variable()
  >>> opti.minimize((x-3)**2)
  >>> con = x <= 1
  >>> opti.subject_to(con)
  >>> opti.solver(\"ipopt\", {\"print_time\": False}, {\"print_level\": 0, \"sb\": \"yes\"})
  >>> sol = opti.solve()
  >>> round(sol.value(opti.dual(con)), 4), round(sol.value(opti.lam_g), 4)
  (4.0, 4.0)
  >>> opti.subject_to()
  >>> con = x >= 4
  >>> opti.subject_to(con)
  >>> sol = opti.solve()
  >>> round(sol.value(opti.dual(con)), 4), round(sol.value(opti.lam_g), 4)
  (2.0, -2.0)
  >>> try:
  ...   opti.dual(x >= 4)
  ... except Exception as e:
  ...   print(str(e).splitlines()[-1])
  Constraint not present in Opti stack.
  





See also: lam_g

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_1h

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/optistack.hpp#L1142
Implementation:
