%feature("docstring")  casadi::Opti::update_user_dict(const MX &m, const
Dict &meta) "

Add user data to a symbol or constraint.

Merges ``meta`` into the dict attached to a variable, parameter, dual
variable (or every symbol of an expression) or to a constraint expression
passed to subject_to(). Opti itself stores a \"stacktrace\" entry there in
Python and MATLAB, which is what describe()/x_describe() print as \"called
from\".



Parameters:
    m: Symbol, expression of symbols, or constraint expression
    meta: Dict entries to add (existing keys are overwritten)



::

  >>> opti = Opti()
  >>> x = opti.variable()
  >>> opti.update_user_dict(x, {\"name\": \"speed\", \"unit\": \"m/s\"})
  >>> d = opti.user_dict(x)
  >>> d[\"name\"], d[\"unit\"], \"stacktrace\" in d
  ('speed', 'm/s', True)
  >>> con = x >= 0
  >>> opti.subject_to(con)
  >>> opti.update_user_dict(con, {\"name\": \"nonneg\"})
  >>> opti.user_dict(con)[\"name\"]
  'nonneg'
  



