%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::combine(const Sparsity &y, bool
f0x_is_zero, bool function0_is_zero, std::vector< unsigned char > &mapping)
const "

Combine two patterns of the same shape, as the result of a binary operation.

Models the pattern of f(x, y) applied elementwise, where ``y`` has this
pattern's shape. An entry is kept in the result when both arguments are
nonzero; an entry where only y is nonzero is kept unless ``f0x_is_zero``
(f(0, y) == 0) and an entry where only x is nonzero is kept unless
``function0_is_zero`` (f(x, 0) == 0). So combine(y, False, False) is the
union (unite) and combine(y, True, True) is the intersection (intersect). A
shape mismatch raises an error.

The C++ overload with ``mapping`` returns, per nonzero of the union, bit 1
if the first argument is nonzero, bit 2 if the second is and bit 4 if the
entry was dropped from the result.



Parameters:
    y: Pattern with the same shape
    f0x_is_zero: True if entries where only ``y`` is nonzero are structural zeros
    function0_is_zero: True if entries where only this pattern is nonzero are structural zeros



::

  >>> a = Sparsity.diag(2)
  >>> b = Sparsity.triplet(2, 2, [0, 1], [1, 1])
  >>> a.combine(b, False, False) == a + b, a.combine(b, True, True) == a * b
  (True, True)
  >>> DM(a.combine(b, True, False), 1)
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [00, 1]])
  >>> DM(a.combine(b, False, True), 1)
  DM(
  [[00, 1],
   [00, 1]])
  





See also: unite, intersect

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_cl

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity.hpp#L2181
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity.cpp#L398-L402
";

