%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::triplet(casadi_int nrow, casadi_int
ncol, const std::vector< casadi_int > &row, const std::vector< casadi_int >
&col, std::vector< casadi_int > &mapping, bool invert_mapping) "

Create a sparsity pattern from the (row, col) index of every nonzero.

The entries may be given in any order; duplicates are merged. An index out
of range or vectors of different length raise an error.



Parameters:
    nrow: Number of rows
    ncol: Number of columns
    row: Row index of each entry, in [0, nrow)
    col: Column index of each entry, in [0, ncol), same length as ``row``
    invert_mapping: Selects the direction of the returned mapping (see below)

The overload with ``invert_mapping`` additionally returns a mapping between
the given entries and the nonzeros of the result (which are in column-major
order). With ``invert_mapping`` false, mapping[k] is the position in the
input of nonzero k (length nnz(); for duplicates the first occurrence). With
``invert_mapping`` true, mapping[i] is the nonzero index of input entry i
(length of the input).



::

  >>> DM(Sparsity.triplet(3, 3, [0, 2, 1], [0, 0, 2]), 1)
  DM(
  [[1, 00, 00],
   [00, 00, 1],
   [1, 00, 00]])
  >>> Sparsity.triplet(2, 2, [0, 0, 1], [0, 0, 1]).nnz()
  2
  >>> sp, mapping = Sparsity.triplet(3, 3, [2, 0, 1], [1, 0, 0], False)
  >>> mapping
  [1, 2, 0]
  >>> sp, mapping = Sparsity.triplet(3, 3, [2, 0, 1], [1, 0, 0], True)
  >>> mapping
  [2, 0, 1]
  >>> try: Sparsity.triplet(2, 2, [0, 2], [0, 0])
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"out of bounds\")
  out of bounds
  





See also: get_triplet, rowcol, nonzeros, Sparsity(nrow, ncol, colind, row)

