https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity.cpp#L1143-L1293
";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::compressed(const std::vector<
casadi_int > &v, bool order_rows=false) "

Create from the compact single-vector representation of a pattern.

The vector is laid out as [nrow, ncol, colind (ncol+1 entries), row
(colind[ncol] entries)]. This is the format returned by compress() and used
by generated C code (casadi_int arrays). When colind[ncol] equals nrow*ncol
the row entries may be omitted (a dense pattern). An inconsistent vector
raises an error.



Parameters:
    v: Compact representation
    order_rows: If true, unsorted row indices within a column are sorted instead of raising an error



::

  >>> sp = Sparsity.compressed([3, 2, 0, 1, 2, 0, 2])
  >>> DM(sp, 1)
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [00, 00],
   [00, 1]])
  >>> Sparsity.compressed(sp.compress()) == sp
  True
  >>> Sparsity.compressed([2, 2, 0, 2, 4])
  Sparsity(2x2)
  





See also: compress, Sparsity(nrow, ncol, colind, row)

