%feature("docstring") casadi::Sparsity::Sparsity(casadi_int nrow, casadi_int
ncol, const std::vector< casadi_int > &colind, const std::vector< casadi_int
> &row, bool order_rows=false) "

Construct from compressed column storage vectors.



Parameters:
    nrow: Number of rows
    ncol: Number of columns
    colind: Column offsets, length ``ncol+1``, colind[0] == 0, nondecreasing
    row: Row index of each nonzero, length colind[ncol], each in [0, nrow), strictly increasing within a column
    order_rows: If true, row indices that are not sorted within a column are sorted (duplicates merged) instead of raising an error

An invalid colind or an out-of-range row index raises an error. A pattern
with colind[ncol] == nrow*ncol is the dense pattern.



::

  >>> sp = Sparsity(3, 2, [0, 2, 3], [0, 2, 1])
  >>> DM(sp, 1)
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [00, 1],
   [1, 00]])
  >>> Sparsity(2, 2, [0, 2, 4], [0, 1, 0, 1]).is_dense()
  True
  >>> try: Sparsity(3, 2, [0, 2, 3], [2, 0, 1])
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"not sorted\")
  not sorted
  >>> Sparsity(3, 2, [0, 2, 3], [2, 0, 1], True).row()
  [0, 2, 1]
  





