%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::get_diag(std::vector< casadi_int >
&mapping) const "

Pattern of the diagonal of a matrix, or of the diagonal matrix built from a
vector.

If the pattern is not a vector, the result is the min(nrow, ncol)-by-1
pattern of the main diagonal: it has a nonzero for every diagonal entry (i,
i) present in the pattern. If the pattern is a row or column vector of
length n, the result is the n-by-n pattern with the vector entries on the
diagonal.



Returns:
    The pattern and a mapping: mapping[k] is the nonzero index in the original pattern of nonzero k of the result



::

  >>> sp, mapping = Sparsity.banded(3, 1).get_diag()
  >>> sp, mapping
  (Sparsity(3x1), [0, 3, 6])
  >>> sp, mapping = Sparsity.unit(3, 1).get_diag()
  >>> DM(sp, 1), mapping
  (DM(
  [[00, 00, 00],
   [00, 1, 00],
   [00, 00, 00]]), [0])
  >>> sp, mapping = Sparsity(2, 3).get_diag()
  >>> sp, mapping
  (Sparsity(2x1,0nz), [])
  





See also: diag, nnz_diag

