%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::compress(bool canonical=true) const
"

Compact single-vector representation of the pattern.

Returns [nrow, ncol, colind..., row...], the layout accepted by compressed()
and used for sparsity patterns in generated C code. With ``canonical``
false, a dense pattern is abbreviated to [nrow, ncol, 1] (an abbreviation
that compressed() given a vector does not accept).



::

  >>> Sparsity.diag(2).compress()
  [2, 2, 0, 1, 2, 0, 1]
  >>> Sparsity.dense(2, 2).compress()
  [2, 2, 0, 2, 4, 0, 1, 0, 1]
  >>> Sparsity.dense(2, 2).compress(False)
  [2, 2, 1]
  >>> Sparsity(0, 2).compress()
