%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::is_stacked(const Sparsity &y,
casadi_int n) const "

Check whether the pattern is ``n`` copies of ``y`` placed side by side.

True when this pattern equals horzcat(y, ..., y) with ``n`` repetitions,
i.e. the pattern of repmat(y, 1, n). The patterns are compared structurally,
so a dense pattern of the right shape does not count as a stack of a sparse
one.



::

  >>> sp = horzcat(Sparsity.diag(2), Sparsity.diag(2), Sparsity.diag(2))
  >>> sp.is_stacked(Sparsity.diag(2), 3), sp.is_stacked(Sparsity.diag(2), 2)
  (True, False)
  >>> Sparsity.dense(2, 6).is_stacked(Sparsity.diag(2), 3)
  False
  





See also: is_equal, horzcat

