%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::to_file(const std::string
&filename, const std::string &format_hint="") const "

Write the pattern to a file.

The only supported format is Matrix Market (\"mtx\", coordinate pattern
general), with one-based (row, col) pairs. The format is taken from the file
extension unless ``format_hint`` is given; an unknown format raises an
error. The file is overwritten.



Parameters:
    filename: Path of the file to write
    format_hint: Format name, e.g. \"mtx\", when the extension does not tell



::

  >>> import os, tempfile
  >>> d = tempfile.mkdtemp()
  >>> f = os.path.join(d, \"pattern.mtx\")
  >>> sp = Sparsity.triplet(3, 2, [0, 2, 1], [0, 0, 1])
  >>> sp.to_file(f)
  >>> print(open(f).read())
  %%MatrixMarket matrix coordinate pattern general
  3 2 3
  1 1
  3 1
  2 2
  >>> print(Sparsity.from_file(f) == sp)
  True
  >>> os.remove(f); os.rmdir(d)
  >>> try: sp.to_file(\"pattern.txt\")
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"unknown extension\")
  unknown extension
  





See also: from_file, DM::to_file

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2ns

