%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::sub(const std::vector< casadi_int >
&rr, const std::vector< casadi_int > &cc, std::vector< casadi_int >
&mapping, bool ind1=false) const "

Pattern of the submatrix with rows ``rr`` and columns ``cc``.

This is the sparsity counterpart of slicing a matrix as A[rr, cc]. Indices
may repeat and may be negative (counting from the end); an index out of
range raises an error.



Parameters:
    rr: Row indices of the submatrix
    cc: Column indices of the submatrix
    ind1: If true, indices are one-based



Returns:
    The len(rr)-by-len(cc) pattern and a mapping with one entry per nonzero of the result: nonzero k of the submatrix is nonzero mapping[k] of this pattern



::

  >>> sp = Sparsity.triplet(3, 4, [0, 2, 1, 0], [0, 0, 2, 3])
  >>> sub, mapping = sp.sub([0, 2], [0, 3])
  >>> DM(sub, 1), mapping
  (DM(
  [[1, 1],
   [1, 00]]), [0, 1, 3])
  >>> sub, mapping = sp.sub([-1], [0])
  >>> sub, mapping
  (Sparsity(1x1), [1])
  >>> sub, mapping = sp.sub([0, 0], [0])
  >>> sub, mapping
  (Sparsity(2x1), [0, 0])
  >>> try: sp.sub([3], [0])
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"out of range\")
  out of range
  





See also: get_nz, erase, pmult

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_ci

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity.hpp#L1920
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity.cpp#L334-L337
";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::sub(const std::vector< casadi_int >
&rr, const Sparsity &sp, std::vector< casadi_int > &mapping, bool
ind1=false) const "

Pattern of a set of elements, arranged according to a given pattern.

``rr`` lists one flat (column-major) element index per nonzero of ``sp``.
The result has the shape of ``sp`` and keeps the nonzeros of ``sp`` whose
element in this pattern is a structural nonzero. This is the sparsity
counterpart of indexing a matrix with a Sparsity or with a list of element
indices.



Parameters:
    rr: Flat element indices, length sp.nnz(); negative indices count from the end, out of range raises an error
    sp: Pattern that lays out the result
    ind1: If true, indices are one-based



Returns:
    The pattern and a mapping: nonzero k of the result is nonzero mapping[k] of this pattern



::

  >>> sp = Sparsity.triplet(3, 4, [0, 2, 1, 0], [0, 0, 2, 3])
  >>> sub, mapping = sp.sub([0, 2, 9], Sparsity.dense(3, 1))
  >>> sub, mapping
  (Sparsity(3x1), [0, 1, 3])
  >>> sub, mapping = sp.sub([0, 1, 2, 3], Sparsity.dense(2, 2))
  >>> DM(sub, 1), mapping
  (DM(
  [[1, 1],
   [00, 00]]), [0, 1])
  >>> try: sp.sub([0, 2], Sparsity.dense(3, 1))
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"length mismatch\")
  length mismatch
  





See also: get_nz, find

