%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::is_compactible(std::vector<
casadi_int > &row, std::vector< casadi_int > &col) const "

Check if the nonzero pattern is the Cartesian product of a row and a column
subset.

If true, returns the (sorted) row and column index sets such that nz(i, j)
<-> i in row and j in col. The nonzero buffer of a compactible matrix in CCS
is laid out exactly as a column-major dense row.size() x col.size() matrix,
so it can be consumed by dense kernels without gather/scatter. The index
sets are returned in either case (the nonempty rows and columns); a pattern
without nonzeros is compactible.



::

  >>> ok, row, col = Sparsity.rowcol([0, 2], [0, 2], 3, 3).is_compactible()
  >>> ok, row, col
  (True, [0, 2], [0, 2])
  >>> ok, row, col = Sparsity.diag(3).is_compactible()
  >>> ok, row, col
  (False, [0, 1, 2], [0, 1, 2])
  





See also: rowcol

