%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::is_subset(const Sparsity &rhs)
const "

Check whether every nonzero of this pattern is also a nonzero of ``rhs``.

Both patterns must have the same shape, otherwise an error is raised. A
pattern is a subset of itself and an all-zero pattern is a subset of any
pattern of its shape.



::

  >>> Sparsity.diag(3).is_subset(Sparsity.dense(3, 3))
  True
  >>> Sparsity.dense(3, 3).is_subset(Sparsity.diag(3))
  False
  >>> Sparsity(3, 3).is_subset(Sparsity.diag(3))
  True
  >>> Sparsity.diag(3).is_subset(Sparsity.diag(3))
  True
  





See also: unite, intersect, is_equal

