%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::enlarge(casadi_int nrow, casadi_int
ncol, const std::vector< casadi_int > &rr, const std::vector< casadi_int >
&cc, bool ind1=false) "

Enlarge the pattern in place by inserting empty rows and columns.

The existing nonzeros are kept and scattered: row i of the old pattern
becomes row rr[i] and column j becomes column cc[j] of the new nrow- by-ncol
pattern, so that B[rr, cc] has the old pattern. The new rows and columns are
structural zeros. Nonzero indices are unchanged. The object is rebound to
the new pattern.



Parameters:
    nrow: New number of rows
    ncol: New number of columns
    rr: New row of every old row: length size1(), strictly increasing, entries in [0, nrow); negative entries count from the end
    cc: New column of every old column: length size2(), strictly increasing, entries in [0, ncol)
    ind1: If true, indices are one-based

A wrong length or an index out of range raises an error.



::

  >>> sp = Sparsity.dense(2, 2)
  >>> sp.enlarge(4, 3, [0, 3], [1, 2])
  >>> DM(sp, 1)
  DM(
  [[00, 1, 1],
   [00, 00, 00],
   [00, 00, 00],
   [00, 1, 1]])
  >>> try: Sparsity.dense(2, 2).enlarge(4, 3, [0], [1, 2])
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"wrong length\")
  wrong length
  





See also: enlargeRows, enlargeColumns, resize, erase

