%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::erase(const std::vector< casadi_int
> &rr, const std::vector< casadi_int > &cc, bool ind1=false) "

Turn the entries with rows ``rr`` and columns ``cc`` into structural zeros,
in place.

The shape is unchanged: only the nonzeros in the block rr x cc are removed.
An entry is removed when its row is in ``rr`` and its column is in ``cc``,
so an empty ``rr`` or ``cc`` removes nothing. Indices may be unsorted and
negative (counting from the end); out of range raises an error. The object
is rebound to the new pattern.



Parameters:
    rr: Rows of the block to clear
    cc: Columns of the block to clear
    ind1: If true, indices are one-based



Returns:
    Mapping of length nnz() of the result: nonzero k of the result was nonzero mapping[k] of the original pattern



::

  >>> sp = Sparsity.dense(3, 3)
  >>> mapping = sp.erase([0, 2], [1])
  >>> DM(sp, 1), mapping
  (DM(
  [[1, 00, 1],
   [1, 1, 1],
   [1, 00, 1]]), [0, 1, 2, 4, 6, 7, 8])
  





See also: erase(rr), sub, enlarge

