%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::is_orthonormal(bool
allow_empty=false) const "

Check whether every row and every column has at most one nonzero.

Without ``allow_empty`` the pattern must also be square with exactly one
nonzero per row and column (a permutation pattern). With ``allow_empty``,
rows and columns without nonzeros are disregarded and the shape may be
rectangular.



Parameters:
    allow_empty: Disregard empty rows and columns in the analysis



::

  >>> Sparsity.diag(3).is_orthonormal()
  True
  >>> Sparsity.triplet(3, 3, [0, 1], [0, 1]).is_orthonormal()
  False
  >>> Sparsity.triplet(3, 3, [0, 1], [0, 1]).is_orthonormal(True)
  True
  >>> Sparsity.triplet(3, 3, [0, 0], [0, 1]).is_orthonormal(True)
  False
  >>> Sparsity.diag(2, 3).is_orthonormal(), Sparsity.diag(2, 3).is_orthonormal(True)
  (False, True)
  





See also: is_orthonormal_rows, is_orthonormal_columns, is_permutation

