%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::etree(bool ata=false) const "

Elimination tree of the pattern.

Returns, for every column, the index of its parent in the elimination tree,
or -1 for a root. See Direct Methods for Sparse Linear Systems by Davis
(2006). With ``ata`` false the result matches MATLAB's etree(A) with zero-
based indices (the pattern is treated as symmetric, only the upper
triangular part is used); with ``ata`` true it matches etree(A, 'col'), the
tree of A'*A.

The implementation is a modified version of cs_etree in CSparse Copyright(c)
Timothy A. Davis, 2006-2009 Licensed as a derivative work under the GNU LGPL



::

  >>> Sparsity.banded(4, 1).etree(), Sparsity.diag(4).etree()
  ([1, 2, 3, -1], [-1, -1, -1, -1])
  >>> Sparsity.dense(2, 3).etree(True)
  [1, 2, -1]
  





See also: ldl, qr_sparse, amd

