%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::pmult(const std::vector< casadi_int
> &p, bool permute_rows=true, bool permute_columns=true, bool
invert_permutation=false) const "

Permute the rows and/or columns of the pattern.

Nonzero (i, j) moves to (p[i], p[j]) when both rows and columns are
permuted, to (p[i], j) for rows only and to (i, p[j]) for columns only. In
matrix terms this is P^T*A*P, P^T*A or A*P with P the matrix of
Sparsity.permutation(p). With ``invert_permutation`` the inverse of p is
used instead, so that pmult(p, True, True, True) is the pattern of A[p, p].



Parameters:
    p: Permutation vector; its length must equal the number of rows (if ``permute_rows``) and the number of columns (if ``permute_columns``)
    permute_rows: Permute the rows
    permute_columns: Permute the columns
    invert_permutation: Use the inverse permutation



::

  >>> A = Sparsity.triplet(3, 3, [0, 1, 2, 0], [1, 2, 0, 0])
  >>> DM(A, 1)
  DM(
  [[1, 1, 00],
   [00, 00, 1],
   [1, 00, 00]])
  >>> p = [2, 0, 1]
  >>> DM(A.pmult(p), 1)
  DM(
  [[00, 1, 00],
   [00, 00, 1],
   [1, 00, 1]])
  >>> P = DM(Sparsity.permutation(p), 1)
  >>> A.pmult(p) == (P.T @ DM(A, 1) @ P).sparsity()
  True
  >>> A.pmult(p, True, True, True) == A.sub(p, p)[0]
  True
  >>> DM(A.pmult(p, True, False), 1)
  DM(
  [[00, 00, 1],
   [1, 00, 00],
   [1, 1, 00]])
  





See also: permutation, sub

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_df

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity.hpp#L3919
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity.cpp#L780-L783
";

