%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::spy_matlab(const std::string
&mfile) const "

Write a MATLAB/Octave script that builds the pattern as a sparse matrix and
calls spy.

The file is overwritten. The script defines a sparse matrix A of ones with
this pattern (see export_code) and ends with spy(A).



Parameters:
    mfile: Path of the.m file to write



::

  >>> import os, tempfile
  >>> d = tempfile.mkdtemp()
  >>> f = os.path.join(d, \"show_pattern.m\")
  >>> Sparsity.diag(2, 3).spy_matlab(f)
  >>> print(open(f).read())
  % This function was automatically generated by CasADi
  A_m = 2;
  A_n = 3;
  A_j = [1, 2];
  A_i = [1, 2];
  A_v = ones(size(A_i));
  A = sparse(A_i, A_j, A_v, A_m, A_n);
  spy(A);
  >>> os.remove(f); os.rmdir(d)
  





