%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::export_code(const std::string
&lang, std::ostream &stream=casadi::uout(), const Dict &options=Dict())
const "

Write code that reconstructs the pattern in another language.

Only \"matlab\" is supported: the code defines the dimensions, one- based
column and row indices and the nonzero values of a sparse matrix. The code
is written to the standard output or to the given stream.



Parameters:
    lang: Target language, must be \"matlab\"
    options: Dictionary with \"name\": name of the generated variable (default \"sp\") \"as_matrix\": also emit \"<name> = sparse(...)\" (default true) \"nonzeros\": list of strings used as the nonzero values (default: ones) \"indent_level\": number of two-space indents (default 0) \"inline\": not supported, true raises an error
        \"name\": name of the generated variable (default \"sp\")
        \"as_matrix\": also emit \"<name> = sparse(...)\" (default true)
        \"nonzeros\": list of strings used as the nonzero values (default: ones)
        \"indent_level\": number of two-space indents (default 0)
        \"inline\": not supported, true raises an error

An unknown option raises an error.



::

  >>> Sparsity.diag(2, 3).export_code(\"matlab\")
  sp_m = 2;
  sp_n = 3;
  sp_j = [1, 2];
  sp_i = [1, 2];
  sp_v = ones(size(sp_i));
  sp = sparse(sp_i, sp_j, sp_v, sp_m, sp_n);
  >>> opts = {\"name\": \"A\", \"as_matrix\": False, \"nonzeros\": [\"1.5\", \"2\"]}
  >>> Sparsity.diag(2).export_code(\"matlab\", opts)
  A_m = 2;
  A_n = 2;
  A_j = [1, 2];
  A_i = [1, 2];
  A_v = [1.5, 2];
  >>> try: Sparsity.diag(2).export_code(\"python\")
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"unsupported language\")
  unsupported language
  





