%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::band(casadi_int n, casadi_int p) "

Create a single band in a square sparsity pattern.

The nonzeros are the entries (i+p, i): band(n, 0) equals diag(n), band(n, 1)
is the first subdiagonal and band(n, -1) the first superdiagonal.



Parameters:
    n: Size of the square pattern
    p: Offset of the band from the diagonal, positive below the diagonal and negative above it; |p| must be smaller than ``n``, otherwise an error is raised



::

  >>> DM(Sparsity.band(4, 1), 1)
  DM(
  [[00, 00, 00, 00],
   [1, 00, 00, 00],
   [00, 1, 00, 00],
   [00, 00, 1, 00]])
  >>> DM(Sparsity.band(4, -2), 1)
  DM(
  [[00, 00, 1, 00],
   [00, 00, 00, 1],
   [00, 00, 00, 00],
   [00, 00, 00, 00]])
  >>> Sparsity.band(4, 0) == Sparsity.diag(4)
  True
  





See also: banded, diag

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_bj

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity.hpp#L580
