%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::nonzeros(casadi_int nrow,
casadi_int ncol, const std::vector< casadi_int > &nz, bool ind1=SWIG_IND1) "

Create a sparsity pattern from the flat (column-major) index of every
nonzero.

Inverse of find(): Sparsity.nonzeros(sp.size1(), sp.size2(), sp.find())
equals sp. Duplicates are merged.



Parameters:
    nrow: Number of rows, must be positive
    ncol: Number of columns
    nz: Flat indices, each in [0, nrow*ncol); an index out of range raises an error
    ind1: If true, the indices are one-based



::

  >>> DM(Sparsity.nonzeros(3, 2, [0, 4]), 1)
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [00, 1],
   [00, 00]])
  >>> sp = Sparsity.banded(3, 1)
  >>> Sparsity.nonzeros(3, 3, sp.find()) == sp
  True
  >>> Sparsity.nonzeros(3, 2, [1, 5], True) == Sparsity.nonzeros(3, 2, [0, 4])
  True
  





See also: find, triplet

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_23g

