%feature("docstring")  casadi::Sparsity::kkt(const Sparsity &H, const
Sparsity &J, bool with_x_diag=true, bool with_lam_g_diag=true) "

Pattern of a KKT system [H + I1, J'; J, I2].

Block pattern of the KKT matrix of an NLP with Hessian ``H`` (square,
n-by-n) and constraint Jacobian ``J`` (m-by-n), where I1 and I2 are the
n-by-n and m-by-m diagonal patterns that are included on request. Shape
(n+m)-by-(n+m).



Parameters:
    H: Hessian pattern, must be square
    J: Jacobian pattern, its number of columns must equal the size of ``H``
    with_x_diag: Add the diagonal to the H block
    with_lam_g_diag: Make the lower right block diagonal instead of all-zero



::

  >>> DM(Sparsity.kkt(Sparsity.diag(2), Sparsity.dense(1, 2)), 1)
  DM(
  [[1, 00, 1],
   [00, 1, 1],
   [1, 1, 1]])
  >>> DM(Sparsity.kkt(Sparsity(2, 2), Sparsity.dense(1, 2), False, False), 1)
  DM(
  [[00, 00, 1],
   [00, 00, 1],
   [1, 1, 00]])
  >>> try: Sparsity.kkt(Sparsity.diag(2), Sparsity.dense(1, 3))
  ... except Exception as e: print(\"dimension mismatch\")
  dimension mismatch
  





See also: blockcat

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_dk

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity.hpp#L4214
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity.cpp#L2052-L2067
";


