%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::blocksplit(const
MatType &x, const std::vector< casadi_int > &vert_offset, const std::vector<
casadi_int > &horz_offset) "

Split a matrix into a grid of blocks.

The rows are split at ``vert_offset`` and every row block is then split at
``horz_offset``. Both offset lists follow the rules of vertsplit and
horzsplit: start at 0, non-decreasing, end at the row (column) count.
Inverse of blockcat: blockcat(blocksplit(x, vert_offset, horz_offset)) == x.



Parameters:
    x: Matrix (or Sparsity) to split; any shape
    vert_offset: Row boundaries of the block rows
    horz_offset: Column boundaries of the block columns



Returns:
    List of block rows, each a list of matrices of the same type as ``x``



::

  >>> x = DM([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8, 9]])
  >>> blocksplit(x, [0, 1, 3], [0, 2, 3])
  [[DM([[1, 2]]), DM(3)], [DM(
  [[4, 5],
   [7, 8]]), DM([6, 9])]]
  





See also: blockcat, vertsplit, horzsplit

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_3n

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L596
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L596-L600
";

