%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::veccat(const
std::vector< MatType > &x) "

Concatenate vertically after vectorizing every argument.

Every argument is first turned into a column with vec (column-major), then
the columns are stacked. Arguments can have any shape, so this is the common
way to collect decision variables into one vector. With no arguments the
result is a 0-by-1 matrix.



Parameters:
    x: List of matrices of any shape



Returns:
    Column vector of the same type as the arguments



::

  >>> veccat(DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]), 5)
  DM([1, 3, 2, 4, 5])
  >>> veccat(MX.sym(\"x\", 2, 2), MX.sym(\"y\", 1, 3))
  MX(vertcat(vec(x), y'))
  >>> veccat().shape
  (0, 1)
  





See also: vec, vertcat

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_3u

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L877
