%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::vec(const MatType
&x) "

Reshape a matrix into a column vector.

Stacks the columns of ``x`` on top of each other (column-major order),
giving a column of length x.numel(). Same as reshape(x, x.numel(), 1); a
column is returned unchanged. The sparsity pattern is carried along: no
entries are densified.

a c b d turns into

a b c d

::

  >>> vec(DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]))
  DM([1, 3, 2, 4])
  >>> vec(DM.eye(2))
  DM([1, 00, 00, 1])
  >>> vec(MX.sym(\"x\", 1, 3))
  MX(x')
  





See also: veccat, reshape

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_3z

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L1087
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L1087-L1089
";

