%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::repmat(const MatType
&A, casadi_int n, casadi_int m=1) "

Repeat matrix A n times vertically and m times horizontally.

Tiles ``A`` into an n-by-m grid of copies; the sparsity pattern is tiled
along. A zero count gives an empty matrix with the remaining dimension kept.
For MX the horizontal repetition is a single node, the vertical one a
vertcat of ``n`` references.



Parameters:
    A: Matrix (or Sparsity) to tile; any shape
    n: Number of vertical repetitions, non-negative
    m: Number of horizontal repetitions, non-negative



::

  >>> repmat(DM([[1, 2]]), 2, 2)
  DM(
  [[1, 2, 1, 2],
   [1, 2, 1, 2]])
  >>> repmat(DM.eye(2), 1, 2)
  DM(
  [[1, 00, 1, 00],
   [00, 1, 00, 1]])
  >>> repmat(MX.sym(\"x\", 2), 1, 3)
  MX(repmat(x, 3))
  >>> repmat(MX.sym(\"x\", 2), 3, 1)
  MX(vertcat(x, x, x))
  >>> repmat(DM.ones(2, 3), 0, 2).shape
  (0, 6)
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_48

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L1469
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L1469-L1471
";

