%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::diagsplit(const
MatType &x, const std::vector< casadi_int > &output_offset1, const
std::vector< casadi_int > &output_offset2) "

Split a matrix into diagonal blocks of given row and column boundaries.

Block i is ``x``[output_offset1[i]:output_offset1[i+1],
output_offset2[i]:output_offset2[i+1]]. Both lists must have the same
length, start at 0, be non-decreasing and end at the row (column) count of
``x``. Entries of ``x`` outside the diagonal blocks are dropped for DM, SX
and Sparsity; for MX they must be structurally zero, otherwise an error is
raised. Inverse of diagcat: diagcat(diagsplit(x, ...)) == x for block-
diagonal ``x``.



Parameters:
    x: Matrix (or Sparsity) to split; any shape
    output_offset1: Row boundaries of the blocks
    output_offset2: Column boundaries of the blocks



Returns:
    List of matrices of the same type as ``x``, one per block



::

  >>> x = DM([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]])
  >>> diagsplit(x, [0, 1, 2], [0, 2, 3])
  [DM([[1, 2]]), DM(6)]
  





See also: diagcat

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_3q

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L725
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L725-L729
";

