%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::horzsplit(const
MatType &x, casadi_int incr=1) "

Split a matrix horizontally into fixed-size groups of columns.

Returns the consecutive column blocks of ``x``, each with ``incr`` columns,
in order. The last block is smaller when the column count is not a multiple
of ``incr``. A matrix without columns gives an empty list. Each block
carries the corresponding part of the sparsity pattern. Inverse of horzcat:
horzcat(horzsplit(x, incr)) == x.



Parameters:
    x: Matrix (or Sparsity) to split; any shape
    incr: Number of columns per block, must be positive



Returns:
    List of matrices of the same type as ``x``



::

  >>> horzsplit(SX.sym(\"x\", 1, 3))
  [SX(x_0), SX(x_1), SX(x_2)]
  >>> horzsplit(DM([[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]]), 2)
  [DM([[1, 2]]), DM([[3, 4]]), DM(5)]
  >>> horzsplit(MX.sym(\"x\", 2, 4), 2)
  [MX(horzsplit(x){0}), MX(horzsplit(x){1})]
  >>> horzsplit(Sparsity.diag(3), 2)
  [Sparsity(3x2,2nz), Sparsity(3x1,1nz)]
  >>> horzsplit(MX.sym(\"x\", 2, 0))
  []
  





See also: horzsplit_n, vertsplit

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_3h

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L299
Implementation:
