%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::vertsplit(const
MatType &x, const std::vector< casadi_int > &offset) "

Split a matrix vertically into groups of rows.

Returns the row blocks ``x``[offset[i]:offset[i+1], :], in order. The
offsets must start at 0, be non-decreasing and end at the number of rows of
``x``, otherwise an error is raised. Each block carries the corresponding
part of the sparsity pattern. The offsets of a list of matrices that were
stacked with vertcat can be recovered with offset. Inverse of vertcat:
vertcat(vertsplit(x, offset)) == x.



Parameters:
    x: Matrix (or Sparsity) to split; any shape
    offset: Start row of every block followed by the row count of ``x``



Returns:
    List of matrices of the same type as ``x``, one per block



::

  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\", 5)
  >>> vertsplit(x, [0, 2, 5])
  [SX([x_0, x_1]), SX([x_2, x_3, x_4])]
  >>> parts = [DM.ones(2, 1), DM.ones(3, 1)]
  >>> vertsplit(x, offset(parts))
  [SX([x_0, x_1]), SX([x_2, x_3, x_4])]
  >>> vertsplit(DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]), [0, 1, 2])
  [DM([[1, 2]]), DM([[3, 4]])]
  





See also: vertsplit_n, horzsplit, offset

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_3i

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L381
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L381-L383
";

