%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::vertsplit(const
MatType &x, casadi_int incr=1) "

Split a matrix vertically into fixed-size groups of rows.

Returns the consecutive row blocks of ``x``, each with ``incr`` rows, in
order. The last block is smaller when the row count is not a multiple of
``incr``. A matrix without rows gives an empty list. Each block carries the
corresponding part of the sparsity pattern. Inverse of vertcat:
vertcat(vertsplit(x, incr)) == x.



Parameters:
    x: Matrix (or Sparsity) to split; any shape
    incr: Number of rows per block, must be positive



Returns:
    List of matrices of the same type as ``x``



::

  >>> vertsplit(SX.sym(\"a\", 4))
  [SX(a_0), SX(a_1), SX(a_2), SX(a_3)]
  >>> vertsplit(SX.sym(\"a\", 4), 2)
  [SX([a_0, a_1]), SX([a_2, a_3])]
  >>> vertsplit(DM([0, 1, 2, 3, 4]), 2)
  [DM([0, 1]), DM([2, 3]), DM(4)]
  >>> vertsplit(MX.sym(\"x\", 4), 2)
  [MX(vertsplit(x){0}), MX(vertsplit(x){1})]
  >>> vertsplit(MX.sym(\"x\", 0, 2))
  []
  





See also: vertsplit_n, horzsplit

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_3k

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L457
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L457-L459
";

