%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::horzsplit_n(const
MatType &x, casadi_int n) "

Split a matrix horizontally into a given number of equal groups of columns.

Returns ``n`` column blocks of equal width, in order. An error is raised
when the column count of ``x`` is not a multiple of ``n`` or ``n`` is
negative. A matrix without columns gives ``n`` copies of itself. Inverse of
horzcat: horzcat(horzsplit_n(x, n)) == x.



Parameters:
    x: Matrix (or Sparsity) to split; any shape
    n: Number of blocks



Returns:
    List of ``n`` matrices of the same type as ``x``



::

  >>> horzsplit_n(DM([[1, 2, 3, 4]]), 2)
  [DM([[1, 2]]), DM([[3, 4]])]
  >>> horzsplit_n(DM(2, 0), 3)
  [DM(2x0), DM(2x0), DM(2x0)]
  >>> horzsplit_n(DM([[1, 2, 3]]), 2)
  Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
  RuntimeError: ...must be a multiple of n...
  





See also: horzsplit, vertsplit_n

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_277

