%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::horzcat(const
std::vector< MatType > &v) "

Concatenate a list of matrices horizontally.

Places the matrices side by side, in order: the result has the row count of
the inputs and a column count equal to the sum of the column counts. All
inputs must have the same number of rows; a 0-by-0 matrix is ignored. The
result is of the type of the arguments, numeric arguments are converted to
the symbolic type (DM mixes with SX or MX, but SX and MX cannot be mixed).
The sparsity pattern of each block is preserved. With no arguments the
result is a 1-by-0 matrix.

Alternative terminology: horizontal stack, hstack, horizontal append, [a b].
Inverse of horzsplit: horzcat(horzsplit(x, ...)) == x.



Parameters:
    v: List of matrices with matching row count



Returns:
    Matrix with the blocks of ``v`` side by side



::

  >>> horzcat(DM([1, 2]), DM([3, 4]), DM([5, 6]))
  DM(
  [[1, 3, 5],
   [2, 4, 6]])
  >>> horzcat(SX.sym(\"x\", 2), DM.ones(2, 1))
  SX(@1=1,
  [[x_0, @1],
   [x_1, @1]])
  >>> horzcat(MX.sym(\"x\", 2, 2), MX.sym(\"y\", 2, 0))
  MX(x)
  >>> horzcat().shape, horzcat(DM(2, 3), DM(0, 0)).shape
  ((1, 0), (2, 3))
  >>> horzcat(DM.ones(2, 2), DM.ones(3, 1))
  Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
  RuntimeError: ...Mismatching number of rows...
  





See also: vertcat, diagcat, veccat, horzsplit

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_3e

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L144
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L144-L146
";

