%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::vertcat(const
std::vector< MatType > &v) "

Concatenate a list of matrices vertically.

Stacks the matrices on top of each other, in order: the result has the
column count of the inputs and a row count equal to the sum of the row
counts. All inputs must have the same number of columns; a 0-by-0 matrix is
ignored. Type and sparsity rules are those of horzcat. With no arguments the
result is a 0-by-1 matrix.

Column vectors stack cheaply; for MX, stacking matrices with more than one
column is rewritten as a horizontal concatenation of the transposes.

Alternative terminology: vertical stack, vstack, vertical append, [a;b].
Inverse of vertsplit: vertcat(vertsplit(x, ...)) == x.



Parameters:
    v: List of matrices with matching column count



Returns:
    Matrix with the blocks of ``v`` stacked vertically



::

  >>> vertcat(SX.sym(\"x\", 2), 3)
  SX([x_0, x_1, 3])
  >>> vertcat(DM([[1, 2]]), DM.eye(2))
  DM(
  [[1, 2],
   [1, 00],
   [00, 1]])
  >>> vertcat(MX.sym(\"a\", 2, 3), MX.sym(\"b\", 1, 3))
  MX(horzcat(a', b')')
  >>> vertcat().shape
  (0, 1)
  >>> vertcat(MX.sym(\"a\", 2, 2), MX.sym(\"b\", 2, 3))
  Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
  RuntimeError: ...vertcat dimension mismatch...
  





See also: horzcat, diagcat, veccat, vertsplit

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_3f

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L198
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L198-L200
";

