%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::blockcat(const
std::vector< std::vector< MatType > > &v) "

Construct a matrix from a list of lists of blocks.

Each inner list is a block row: its entries are concatenated horizontally,
and the resulting block rows are concatenated vertically. The usual
concatenation rules apply: blocks in one block row need the same number of
rows, block rows need the same total number of columns, otherwise an error
is raised. Inverse of blocksplit: blockcat(blocksplit(x, ...)) == x.



Parameters:
    v: List of block rows, each a list of matrices



Returns:
    Matrix of the same type as the blocks



::

  >>> blockcat([[DM(1), DM([[2, 3]])], [DM([4, 5]), DM.eye(2)]])
  DM(
  [[1, 2, 3],
   [4, 1, 00],
   [5, 00, 1]])
  >>> a, b, c, d = MX.sym(\"a\", 2, 2), MX.sym(\"b\", 2, 1), MX.sym(\"c\", 1, 2), MX.sym(\"d\")
  >>> blockcat([[a, b], [c, d]])
  MX(horzcat(horzcat(a, b)', horzcat(c, d)')')
  





See also: horzcat, vertcat, blocksplit

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_3l

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L533
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L533-L535
";

