%feature("docstring") casadi::casadi_diagcat "

Construct a block-diagonal matrix from a list of matrices.

Places the matrices along the diagonal, in order; all other entries are
structural zeros. The blocks need not be square: the result has the sum of
the row counts by the sum of the column counts. Type rules are those of
horzcat. With no arguments the result is a 0-by-0 matrix. Inverse of
diagsplit: diagcat(diagsplit(x, ...)) == x.



Parameters:
    A: List of matrices of any shape



Returns:
    Block-diagonal matrix of the same type as the blocks



::

  >>> diagcat(DM.ones(1, 2), 3)
  DM(
  [[1, 1, 00],
   [00, 00, 3]])
  >>> diagcat(SX.sym(\"x\"), SX.sym(\"y\", 2))
  SX(
  [[x, 00],
   [00, y_0],
   [00, y_1]])
  >>> diagcat(MX.sym(\"x\"), MX.sym(\"y\", 2, 2))
  MX(diagcat(x, y))
  >>> diagcat().shape
  (0, 0)
  





See also: horzcat, vertcat, diagsplit

