%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::mac(const MatType
&x, const MatType &y, const MatType &z, const std::string &blas="reference")
"

Multiply-accumulate operation.

Matrix product of two matrices (x and y), adding the result to a third
matrix z. The result has the same sparsity pattern as ``z``, meaning that
other entries of the product are ignored. The operation is equivalent to z +
project(mtimes(x, y), z.sparsity()). The dimensions of ``z`` must match the
product, otherwise an error is raised. When ``x`` or ``y`` is a scalar the
result is z + x*y. See ``mtimes`` for the meaning of the ``blas`` argument.

mtimes is implemented as mac with a structurally zero ``z`` of the product
pattern.



Parameters:
    x: Left factor
    y: Right factor
    z: Matrix to add to; its sparsity pattern selects the computed entries



Returns:
    Matrix with the sparsity pattern of ``z``



::

  >>> A = DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]])
  >>> mac(A, A, DM.eye(2))
  DM(
  [[8, 00],
   [00, 23]])
  >>> mac(A, A, DM.ones(2, 2))
  DM(
  [[8, 11],
   [16, 23]])
  >>> mac(MX.sym(\"x\", 2, 3), MX.sym(\"y\", 3, 2), MX.sym(\"z\", Sparsity.diag(2)))
  MX(mac(x,y,z))
  





See also: mtimes

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_3x

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L1018
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L1018-L1021
";

