%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::reshape(const
MatType &x, casadi_int nrow, casadi_int ncol) "

Returns a reshaped version of the matrix.

Reinterprets the entries of ``x`` in column-major order as a matrix of
``nrow`` by ``ncol``, as reshape does in MATLAB and numpy with order='F'.
The number of elements must not change, otherwise an error is raised. One of
the dimensions can be -1, it is then inferred from the other. The sparsity
pattern is reshaped along; no entries are densified. For MX this is a cheap
reordering node.



Parameters:
    x: Matrix (or Sparsity) to reshape; any shape
    nrow: Number of rows of the result, or -1
    ncol: Number of columns of the result, or -1



::

  >>> x = DM([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]])
  >>> reshape(x, 3, 2)
  DM(
  [[1, 5],
   [4, 3],
   [2, 6]])
  >>> reshape(x, -1, 1)
  DM([1, 4, 2, 5, 3, 6])
  >>> reshape(DM.eye(2), 1, 4)
  DM([[1, 00, 00, 1]])
  >>> reshape(MX.sym(\"x\", 2, 3), 3, 2)
  MX(reshape(x))
  >>> reshape(x, 4, 2)
  Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
  RuntimeError: ...number of elements must remain the same...
  





See also: vec, sparsity_cast, transpose

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_40

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L1141
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/sparsity_interface.hpp#L1141-L1143
";

