%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::triu(const MatType
&x, bool includeDiagonal=true) "

Get the upper triangular part of a matrix.

Entries below the diagonal become structural zeros; the matrix need not be
square. For MX this is a projection node.



Parameters:
    x: Matrix (or Sparsity); any shape
    includeDiagonal: False to drop the diagonal as well



::

  >>> x = DM([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]])
  >>> triu(x)
  DM(
  [[1, 2, 3],
   [00, 5, 6]])
  >>> triu(x, False)
  DM(
  [[00, 2, 3],
   [00, 00, 6]])
  >>> triu(MX.sym(\"x\", 2, 2))
  MX(project(x))
  





See also: tril

