%feature("docstring")  casadi::SparsityInterfaceCommon::sum(const MatType
&x) "

Sum all elements.

Returns a 1-by-1 matrix with the sum of all elements, combining sum1 and
sum2. An empty matrix sums to a structural zero. The Python function also
accepts an axis argument: sum(x, 0) is sum1(x) and sum(x, 1) is sum2(x).



::

  >>> sum(DM([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]]))
  DM(21)
  >>> sum(DM([[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]]), 0)
  DM([[5, 7, 9]])
  >>> sum(SX.sym(\"x\", 3))
  SX(((x_0+x_1)+x_2))
  >>> sum(DM(3, 0))
  DM(00)
  





See also: sum1, sum2

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2d6

