%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericExpressionCommon::times(const SXElem
&x, const SXElem &y) "

Elementwise multiplication: (x,y) -> x .* y.

Elementwise (Hadamard) product, not the matrix product; use mtimes for that.
Shape rules as for plus. The result is structurally zero wherever either
operand is, so the sparsity pattern is the intersection of the patterns.



::

  >>> times(DM([1, 2]), DM([3, 4]))
  DM([3, 8])
  >>> DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]]) * DM([[1, 2], [3, 4]])
  DM(
  [[1, 4],
   [9, 16]])
  >>> DM.eye(2) * DM.ones(2, 2)
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [00, 1]])
  





See also: mtimes

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_op

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L219
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L219-L221
";

