%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericExpressionCommon::logic_not(const
SXElem &x) "

Logical ``not`` x -> !x.

Returns (an expression evaluating to) 1 where the entry is zero and 0
otherwise, elementwise

Structural zeros map to 1, so a sparse input gives a dense result. The
Python keyword ``not`` does not work on matrices; use this function.



::

  >>> logic_not(DM([1, 0, -1]))
  DM([0, 1, 0])
  >>> logic_not(DM.eye(2))
  DM(
  [[0, 1],
   [1, 0]])
  >>> logic_not(SX.sym(\"x\"))
  SX((!x))
  





See also: logic_and, logic_or

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_oz

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L632
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L632-L634
";

