%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericExpressionCommon::eq(const SXElem &x,
const SXElem &y) "

Logical equal to: (x,y) -> x == y.

Elementwise comparison with 0/1 result, see lt: this is value equality of
the entries, not identity of expressions; use is_equal to test whether two
symbolic expressions are the same. For symbolic operands x == x with the
same node simplifies to 1. NaN is not equal to anything, including itself.



::

  >>> eq(DM([1, 2, 3]), 2)
  DM([0, 1, 0])
  >>> DM.eye(2) == DM([[1, 0], [0, 1]])
  DM(
  [[1, 1],
   [1, 1]])
  >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\")
  >>> x == x, x == SX.sym(\"x\")
  (SX(1), SX((x==x)))
  >>> DM(float(\"nan\")) == DM(float(\"nan\"))
  DM(0)
  





See also: ne, is_equal

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_ov

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L471
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L471-L473
";

