%feature("docstring")  casadi::GenericExpressionCommon::abs(const SXElem &x)
"

Absolute value: x -> abs(x)

Elementwise; structural zeros are preserved. The unary functions of this
group operate on every entry, keep the shape and build a symbolic expression
for SX and MX. Those that map 0 to 0 (abs, sqrt, sin, tan, atan, asin, sinh,
tanh, asinh, atanh, floor, ceil, sign, erf, erfinv, log1p, expm1) keep the
sparsity pattern; the others (cos, cosh, exp, log, log10, acos, acosh,
logic_not) return a dense result. Named fabs in Python, where the built-in
abs also applies.



::

  >>> fabs(DM([-1, 0, 2]))
  DM([1, 0, 2])
  >>> fabs(DM.eye(2) * -1)
  DM(
  [[1, 00],
   [00, 1]])
  >>> abs(SX.sym(\"x\"))
  SX(fabs(x))
  





See also: sign, copysign

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_p0

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L677
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L677-L679
";

