Square root: x -> sqrt(x)

Elementwise; sparsity preserved. A negative argument gives NaN, no error is
raised. A symbolic power x**0.5 simplifies to sqrt(x).



::

  >>> sqrt(DM([4, 9]))
  DM([2, 3])
  >>> SX.sym(\"x\")**0.5
  SX(sqrt(x))
  





See also: sq, pow

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_p1

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L711
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/generic_expression.hpp#L711-L713
";

