"

Square: x -> x^2.

Elementwise; sparsity preserved. Not exposed as a function in Python; a
symbolic power with exponent 2 is turned into this operation.



::

  >>> SX.sym(\"x\")**2
  SX(sq(x))
  





See also: sqrt, pow

