erk
---



Explicit Runge-Kutta integrator for ODEs: a pair of order 5(4) with adaptive
or fixed steps, or the classical method of order 4 with fixed steps.

Steps are independent of the output times. Adaptive steps are chosen by
error control on the nominal states; with fixed steps, each run of steps
over a control group (or up to the end) is divided into equal steps of at
most step_size. Outputs inside a step come from a dense output (order 4 and
3 respectively) at no extra cost. Forward sensitivities are the exact
derivatives of the discrete solution and adjoint sensitivities are the exact
discrete adjoint of the taped steps. With fixed steps the tape has a known
bound, so adjoints can be code-generated; with adaptive steps, set
max_tape_steps.

Zero-crossing events (DAE output zero, option transition) are located on the
dense output of the step in which a function becomes negative; integration
restarts from the state after the transition. Sensitivities, forward,
adjoint and forward-over-adjoint, include those of the event times.

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2kb

>List of available options

+--------------------+--------------+--------------------------------------+
|         Id         |     Type     |             Description              |
+====================+==============+======================================+
| abstol             | OT_DOUBLE    | Absolute tolerance [1e-8]            |
+--------------------+--------------+--------------------------------------+
| control_group_size | OT_INTVECTOR | Number of output intervals in each   |
|                    |              | control group, over which the        |
|                    |              | controls, one column each, are       |
|                    |              | constant: a run of steps [default: 1 |
|                    |              | for each output interval]            |
+--------------------+--------------+--------------------------------------+
| max_num_steps      | OT_INT       | Adaptive steps: maximum number of    |
|                    |              | steps per output interval [10000]    |
+--------------------+--------------+--------------------------------------+
| max_step_size      | OT_DOUBLE    | Adaptive steps: maximum step size    |
|                    |              | [default: unbounded]                 |
+--------------------+--------------+--------------------------------------+
| max_tape_steps     | OT_INT       | Adaptive steps: capacity, in steps,  |
|                    |              | of a tape in the work vector, for    |
|                    |              | adjoint sensitivities; needed for    |
|                    |              | code generation [0: tape of          |
|                    |              | unbounded size]. With fixed steps,   |
|                    |              | the tape is sized exactly.           |
+--------------------+--------------+--------------------------------------+
| method             | OT_STRING    | Runge-Kutta method: 'rk45' (pair of  |
|                    |              | order 5(4), adaptive unless          |
|                    |              | step_size is set) or 'rk4'           |
|                    |              | (classical, order 4, fixed steps     |
|                    |              | only; default step_size (tf -        |
|                    |              | t0)/20) [rk45]                       |
