| step_size          | OT_DOUBLE    | Fixed steps: each run of steps, over |
|                    |              | a control group or up to the end     |
|                    |              | without controls, is divided into    |
|                    |              | equal steps of at most step_size [0: |
|                    |              | adaptive steps]                      |
+--------------------+--------------+--------------------------------------+



--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

rosenbrock
----------



Rosenbrock-Wanner integrator for stiff ODEs and semi-explicit index-1 DAEs,
with adaptive or fixed steps.

An 8-stage, stiffly accurate, L-stable method of order 5 with an embedded
method of order 4. Each step needs one Jacobian and one sparse QR
factorization; the method is linearly implicit, without Newton iterations.
Steps cross the output times within a control group, which are interpolated
by a dense output of order 4. Step sizes are chosen from the nominal
solution only, so forward sensitivities are the exact derivatives of the
discrete solution (internal numerical differentiation) and adjoint
sensitivities are the exact discrete adjoint of the taped steps. With
step_size, each run of steps over a control group is divided into equal
steps instead, and the tape has a known bound.

Zero-crossing events (DAE output zero, option transition) are located on the
dense output of the step in which a function becomes negative; integration
restarts from the state after the transition. Sensitivities, forward,
adjoint and forward-over-adjoint, include those of the event times.

Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2ka

