The text includes the plugin-specific option table.



::

  >>> \"newton iterations\" in doc_rootfinder(\"newton\")
  True
  



Extra doc: https://github.com/casadi/casadi/wiki/L_2ni

Doc source:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/rootfinder.hpp#L107
Implementation:
https://github.com/casadi/casadi/blob/main/casadi/core/rootfinder.cpp#L107-L109
";

%feature("docstring")  casadi::rootfinder(const std::string &name, const
std::string &solver, const SXDict &rfp, const Dict &opts=Dict()) "



Create a solver for rootfinding problems

Returns a Function that solves a system of nonlinear equations g(x, p) = 0
for x, given the parameters p and an initial guess for x. The problem is
given as a dictionary with fields \"x\" (unknowns, dense column vector),
\"g\" (residual, dense column vector of the same size) and optionally \"p\"
(parameters); any other field name is an error. The returned Function has
inputs x0 (the guess) and p, and output x (see rootfinder_in and
rootfinder_out). Omitted inputs are zero.

More generally, the problem is given as a Function [y0, y1, ..., yi, ...,
yn] = F(x0, x1, ..., xj, ..., xm) where input xj is unknown and output yi is
the residual that must be zero. The result is [y0, y1, ..., xj, ..., yn] =
G(x0, x1, ..., xj_guess, ..., xm): the unknown input is replaced by a guess
(its name gets a \"0\" suffix) and the residual output is replaced by the
solution (named like the unknown input); the other inputs and outputs are
passed through. By default j = 0 and i = 0; options \"implicit_input\" and
\"implicit_output\" select other indices. xj and yi must be dense column
vectors of the same size and d(yi)/d(xj) must be structurally and
numerically invertible: a structurally rank-deficient Jacobian is an error
at construction, a singular one makes the plugin fail.

The call can be embedded in an MX expression and differentiated: derivatives
follow from the implicit function theorem, using the linear solver chosen
with \"linear_solver\". \"error_on_fail\" defaults to true: a solve that
does not converge raises; with false the last iterate is returned and
stats() reports \"success\" and \"return_status\".

Options common to all plugins (the plugin options follow in the tables
below):

- \"implicit_input\", \"implicit_output\": indices j and i above (default 0).
- \"linear_solver\", \"linear_solver_options\": Linsol plugin for the Newton steps and the sensitivities (default \"qr\").
- \"jacobian_function\": user-supplied Function for d(yi)/d(xj) (generated by default).
- \"constraints\": list with one entry per unknown, 0 (default) for no constraint, 1 for >= 0, -1 for <= 0, 2 for > 0, -2 for < 0; only honored by plugins that support it (e.g. kinsol), ignored by newton.
- \"expand\", \"print_time\", \"verbose\", \"common_options\", \"specific_options\": as for nlpsol.





::

  * >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); p = SX.sym(\"p\")
  * >>> G = rootfinder(\"G\", \"newton\", {\"x\": x, \"p\": p, \"g\": x**2 - p})
  * >>> G
  * Function(G:(x0,p)->(x) Newton)
  * >>> round(float(G(x0=1, p=2)[\"x\"]), 4), round(float(G(1, 2)), 4)
  * (1.4142, 1.4142)
  * >>> G.stats()[\"success\"], G.stats()[\"return_status\"]
  * (True, 'success')
  * >>> pm = MX.sym(\"p\")
  * >>> dxdp = Function(\"dxdp\", [pm], [jacobian(G(x0=1, p=pm)[\"x\"], pm)])
  * >>> dxdp(4)
  * DM(0.25)
  * >>> f = Function(\"f\", [x, p], [x**2 - p, 3*x], [\"x\", \"p\"], [\"g\", \"h\"])
  * >>> G = rootfinder(\"G\", \"newton\", f)
  * >>> G
  * Function(G:(x0,p)->(x,h) Newton)
  * >>> G(x0=1, p=4)
  * {'h': DM(6), 'x': DM(2)}
  * >>> f = Function(\"f\", [p, x], [3*x, x**2 - p], [\"p\", \"x\"], [\"h\", \"g\"])
  * >>> G = rootfinder(\"G\", \"newton\", f, {\"implicit_input\": 1, \"implicit_output\": 1})
  * >>> G
  * Function(G:(p,x0)->(h,x) Newton)
  * 





::

  * >>> x = SX.sym(\"x\"); p = SX.sym(\"p\")
  * >>> G = rootfinder(\"G\", \"newton\", {\"x\": x, \"p\": p, \"g\": x**2 - p}, {\"max_iter\": 2})
  * >>> try:
  * ...     G(x0=1, p=2)
  * ... except RuntimeError as e:
  * ...     print(\"rootfinder process failed\" in str(e))
  * True
  * >>> opts = {\"max_iter\": 2, \"error_on_fail\": False, \"print_iteration\": False}
  * >>> G = rootfinder(\"G\", \"newton\", {\"x\": x, \"p\": p, \"g\": x**2 - p}, opts)
  * >>> round(float(G(x0=1, p=2)[\"x\"]), 4), G.stats()[\"return_status\"]
  * (1.4167, 'max_iteration_reached')
  * >>> X = SX.sym(\"x\", 2)
  * >>> try:
  * ...     rootfinder(\"G\", \"newton\", {\"x\": X, \"g\": vertcat(X[0] - 1, 1)})
  * ... except RuntimeError as e:
  * ...     print(\"structurally rank-deficient\" in str(e))
  * True
  * >>> try:
  * ...     rootfinder(\"G\", \"newton\", {\"x\": X, \"g\": X[0]})
  * ... except RuntimeError as e:
  * ...     print(\"Dimension mismatch\" in str(e))
  * True
  * 



